[2026-04-15T16:54:48.018Z] [INFO]   "bodyPreview": "{\"model\":\"big-pickle\",\"max_tokens\":100,\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"\\n            Summarize the following conversation into 2 sentences MAX explaining what the assistant did and why. Do not explain the user's input. Do not speak in the third person about the assistant.\\n            <conversation>\\n            [{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"You are an AI issue solver using @link-assistant/agent.\\\\nGeneral guidelines.\\\\n   - When you execute commands and the output becomes large, save the logs to files for easier review.\\\\n   - When running commands, avoid setting a timeout yourself. Let them run as long as needed.\\\\n   - When running sudo commands, especially package installations, run them in the background to avoid timeout issues.\\\\n   - When CI is failing, download the logs locally and investigate them carefully.\\\\n   - When a code or log file has more than 1500 lines, read it in chunks of 1500 lines.\\\\n   - When facing a complex problem, do as much tracing as possible and turn on all verbose modes.\\\\n   - When you create debug, test, or example scripts while fixing an issue, keep them in ./examples and/or ./experiments so you can reuse them later.\\\\n   - When you test assumptions, keep experiment scripts in ./experiments.\\\\n   - When an experiment demonstrates a real-world use case of the software, add it to ./examples.\\\\n   - When you face something extremely hard, use divide and conquer.\\\\nInitial research.\\\\n   - When you start, create a detailed plan for yourself and follow your todo list step by step. Add as many relevant points from these guidelines to the todo list as practical so you can track the work clearly.\\\\n   - When you read issue, read all details and comments thoroughly.\\\\n   - When you see screenshots or images in issue descriptions, pull request descriptions, comments, or discussions, download the image to a local file first, then use the Read tool to view and analyze it. Before reading downloaded images with the Read tool, verify that the file is a valid image rather than HTML by using a CLI tool such as the 'file' command. When the file command shows \\\\\\\"HTML\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\", or \\\\\\\"ASCII text\\\\\\\", the download failed, so do not call Read on that file. When images are from GitHub issues or PRs, such as URLs containing \\\\\\\"github.com/user-attachments\\\\\\\", use: curl -L -H \\\\\\\"Authorization: token $(gh auth token)\\\\\\\" -o <filename> \\\\\\\"<url>\\\\\\\"\\\\n   - When you need issue details, use gh issue view https://github.com/Jhon-Crow/godot-topdown-MVP/issues/1826.\\\\n   - When you need related code, use gh search code --owner Jhon-Crow [keywords].\\\\n   - When you need repo context, read files in your working directory.\\\\n   - When you study related work, study the most recent related pull requests.\\\\n   - When the issue is not defined clearly enough, write a comment with clarifying questions.\\\\n   - When accessing GitHub Gists, use gh gist view command instead of direct URL fetching.\\\\n   - When you are fixing a bug, find the actual root cause first and run as many experiments as needed.\\\\n   - When you are fixing a bug and the code does not have enough tracing or logs, add them and keep them in the code with the default state switched off.\\\\n   - When you need comments on a pull request, note that GitHub has three different comment types with different API endpoints:\\\\n      1. PR review comments (inline code comments): gh api repos/Jhon-Crow/godot-topdown-MVP/pulls/1833/comments --paginate\\\\n      2. PR conversation comments (general discussion): gh api repos/Jhon-Crow/godot-topdown-MVP/issues/1833/comments --paginate\\\\n      3. PR reviews (approve/request changes): gh api repos/Jhon-Crow/godot-topdown-MVP/pulls/1833/reviews --paginate\\\\n      Note: The command \\\\\\\"gh pr view --json comments\\\\\\\" only returns conversation comments and misses review comments.\\\\n   - When you need the latest comments on the issue, use gh api repos/Jhon-Crow/godot-topdown-MVP/issues/1826/comments --paginate.\\\\nSolution development and testing.\\\\n   - When issue is solvable, first create a test that reproduces the problem, then implement the fix.\\\\n   - When coding, commit each atomic step that is useful on its own to the pull request branch so interrupted work remains preserved in the pull request.\\\\n   - When you test:\\\\n      start from testing of small functions using separate scripts;\\\\n      write unit tests with mocks for easy and quick start.\\\\n   - When you test integrations, use existing framework.\\\\n   - When you test solution draft, include automated checks in pr.\\\\n   - When you write or modify tests, consider setting reasonable timeouts at test, suite, and CI job levels so failures surface quickly instead of hanging.\\\\n   - When you see repeated test timeout patterns in CI, investigate the root cause rather than increasing timeouts.\\\\n   - When the issue is unclear, write a comment on the issue with questions.\\\\n   - When you encounter any problems that you are unable to solve yourself, write a comment to the pull request asking for help.\\\\n   - When you need human help, use gh pr comment 1833 --body \\\\\\\"your message\\\\\\\" to comment on existing PR.\\\\nReproducible testing.\\\\n   - When fixing a bug, create a test that reproduces the problem before implementing the fix. When you cannot reproduce the problem, you cannot verify the fix.\\\\n   - When encountering logic bugs, write an automated test that fails due to the bug, then implement the fix to make it pass.\\\\n   - When encountering UI bugs, capture a screenshot showing the problem state, then create a visual regression test or manual verification screenshot after the fix.\\\\n   - When creating tests, prefer minimum reproducible examples, meaning the simplest test case that demonstrates the issue.\\\\n   - When submitting a fix, include in the PR description: (1) how to reproduce the issue, (2) the automated test that verifies the fix, (3) before/after screenshots for UI issues.\\\\n   - When a bug fix does not have a reproducing test, treat the fix as incomplete because regressions can occur later without notice.\\\\nPreparing pull request.\\\\n   - When you code, follow contributing guidelines.\\\\n   - When you commit, write clear message.\\\\n   - When you need examples of style, use gh pr list --repo Jhon-Crow/godot-topdown-MVP --state merged --search [keywords].\\\\n   - When you open pr, describe solution draft and include tests.\\\\n   - When there is a package with version and GitHub Actions workflows for automatic release, update the version in your pull request to prepare for next release.\\\\n   - When you update existing pr 1833, use gh pr edit to modify title and description.\\\\n   - When you finalize the pull request:\\\\n      check that the pull request title and description are updated (the PR may start with a [WIP] prefix and a placeholder description that should be replaced with the actual title and description of the changes),\\\\n      follow style from merged prs for code, title, and description,\\\\n      check that no uncommitted changes corresponding to the original requirements are left behind,\\\\n      check that the default branch is merged into the pull request branch,\\\\n      check that all CI checks are passing if they exist before you finish,\\\\n      check for latest comments on the issue and pull request to ensure no recent feedback was missed,\\\\n      double-check that all changes in the pull request address the original requirements of the issue,\\\\n      check for newly introduced bugs in the pull request by carefully reading gh pr diff,\\\\n      check that no previously existing features were removed without an explicit request in the issue description, issue comments, or pull request comments.\\\\n   - When you finish implementation, use gh pr ready 1833.\\\\nWorkflow and collaboration.\\\\n   - When you check branch, verify with git branch --show-current.\\\\n   - When you push, push only to branch issue-1826-328adfe76998.\\\\n   - When you finish, create a pull request from branch issue-1826-328adfe76998.\\\\n   - When pr 1833 already exists for this branch, update it instead of creating new one.\\\\n   - When you organize workflow, use pull requests instead of direct merges to default branch (main or master).\\\\n   - When you manage commits, preserve commit history for later analysis.\\\\n   - When you contribute, keep repository history forward-moving with regular commits, pushes, and reverts if needed.\\\\n   - When you face conflict that you cannot resolve yourself, ask for help.\\\\n   - When you collaborate, respect branch protections by working only on issue-1826-328adfe76998.\\\\n   - When you mention a result, include the pull request URL or comment URL.\\\\n   - When you need to create pr, remember pr 1833 already exists for this branch.\\\\nSelf review.\\\\n   - When you check your solution draft, run all tests locally.\\\\n   - When you check your solution draft, verify git status shows a clean working tree with no uncommitted changes.\\\\n   - When you compare with repo style, use gh pr diff [number].\\\\n   - When you finalize, confirm code, tests, and description are consistent.\\\\nGitHub CLI command patterns.\\\\n   - When fetching lists from GitHub API, use the --paginate flag to ensure all results are returned (GitHub returns max 30 per page by default).\\\\n   - When listing PR review comments (inline code comments), use gh api repos/OWNER/REPO/pulls/NUMBER/comments --paginate.\\\\n   - When listing PR conversation comments, use gh api repos/OWNER/REPO/issues/NUMBER/comments --paginate.\\\\n   - When listing PR reviews, use gh api repos/OWNER/REPO/pulls/NUMBER/reviews --paginate.\\\\n   - When listing issue comments, use gh api repos/OWNER/REPO/issues/NUMBER/comments --paginate.\\\\n   - When adding PR comment, use gh pr comment NUMBER --body \\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\" --repo OWNER/REPO.\\\\n   - When adding issue comment, use gh issue comment NUMBER --body \\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\" --repo OWNER/REPO.\\\\n   - When viewing PR details, use gh pr view NUMBER --repo OWNER/REPO.\\\\n   - When filtering with jq, use gh api repos/Jhon-Crow/godot-topdown-MVP/pulls/1833/comments --paginate --jq 'reverse | .[0:5]'.\\\\nIssue to solve: https://github.com/Jhon-Crow/godot-topdown-MVP/issues/1826\\\\nYour prepared branch: issue-1826-328adfe76998\\\\nYour prepared working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1776272033963\\\\nYour prepared Pull Request: https://github.com/Jhon-Crow/godot-topdown-MVP/pull/1833\\\\nYour forked repository: konard/Jhon-Crow-godot-topdown-MVP\\\\nOriginal repository (upstream): Jhon-Crow/godot-topdown-MVP\\\\nGitHub Actions on your fork: https://github.com/konard/Jhon-Crow-godot-topdown-MVP/actions?query=branch%3Aissue-1826-328adfe76998\\\\nProceed.\\\"}]},{\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"reasoning\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"We are given an issue to solve: https://github.com/Jhon-Crow/godot-topdown-MVP/issues/1826\\\\n We are on a branch: issue-1826-328adfe76998\\\\n We have a prepared PR: https://github.com/Jhon-Crow/godot-topdown-MVP/pull/1833\\\\n\\\\n Let's first look at the issue details to understand the problem.\\\\n\\\\n We'll use the GitHub CLI to view the issue.\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool-call\\\",\\\"toolCallId\\\":\\\"chatcmpl-tool-be69b8258dd78374\\\",\\\"toolName\\\":\\\"bash\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"command\\\":\\\"gh issue view 1826 --repo Jhon-Crow/godot-topdown-MVP\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"View the issue details\\\"}}]},{\\\"role\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool-result\\\",\\\"toolCallId\\\":\\\"chatcmpl-tool-be69b8258dd78374\\\",\\\"toolName\\\":\\\"bash\\\",\\\"output\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"title:\\\\tupdate unlocks\\\\nstate:\\\\tOPEN\\\\nauthor:\\\\tJhon-Crow (Jhon-Crow)\\\\nlabels:\\\\t\\\\ncomments:\\\\t0\\\\nassignees:\\\\t\\\\nprojects:\\\\t\\\\nmilestone:\\\\t\\\\nnumber:\\\\t1826\\\\n--\\\\nдробовик и наступательная граната должен открываться при прохождении карты Здание на любой ранг (даже на F)\\\\n\\\"}}]},{\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"reasoning\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"We are given an issue: \\\\\\\"update unlocks\\\\\\\" with description in Russian: \\\\\\\"дробовик и наступательная граната должен открываться при прохождении карты Здание на любой ранг (даже на F)\\\\\\\"\\\\nTranslation: \\\\\\\"Shotgun and offensive grenade should be unlocked when passing the Building map on any rank (even F)\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nWe need to understand the current unlocking mechanism and change it so that the shotgun and offensive grenade are unlocked upon completing the Building map (level) regardless of the rank (even if the rank is F).\\\\n\\\\nWe are in a Godot project. We should look for where unlocks are handled, likely in the level completion or in a save/data manager.\\\\n\\\\nLet's first explore the repository structure to understand the codebase.\\\\n\\\\nWe'll start by listing the directories and then look for relevant files.\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool-call\\\",\\\"toolCallId\\\":\\\"chatcmpl-tool-ba0760bc4fe7ac5a\\\",\\\"toolName\\\":\\\"bash\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"command\\\":\\\"find . -type f -name \\\\\\\"*.gd\\\\\\\" | grep -E \\\\\\\"(level|building|unlock|shotgun|grenade)\\\\\\\" | head -20\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Search for GDScript files related to level, building, unlock, shotgun, grenade\\\"}}]},{\\\"role\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool-result\\\",\\\"toolCallId\\\":\\\"chatcmpl-tool-ba0760bc4fe7ac5a\\\",\\\"toolName\\\":\\\"bash\\\",\\\"output\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"./docs/case-studies/issue-991/tutorial_level.gd\\\\n./docs/case-studies/issue-991/labyrinth_level.gd\\\\n./scripts/levels/arena_level.gd\\\\n./scripts/levels/sewer_level.gd\\\\n./scripts/levels/labyrinth2_level.gd\\\\n./scripts/levels/revolver_level.gd\\\\n./scripts/levels/test_tier.gd\\\\n./scripts/levels/winter_forest_level.gd\\\\n./scripts/levels/docks_level.gd\\\\n./scripts/levels/roguelike_level.gd\\\\n./scripts/levels/factory_level.gd\\\\n./scripts/levels/beach_level.gd\\\\n./scripts/levels/tutorial_level.gd\\\\n./scripts/levels/castle_level.gd\\\\n./scripts/levels/building_level.gd\\\\n./scripts/levels/labyrinth_level.gd\\\\n./scripts/levels/decadence_level.gd\\\\n./scripts/levels/city_level.gd\\\\n./scripts/levels/railway_station_level.gd\\\\n./scripts/ui/unlock_table_menu.gd\\\\n\\\"}}]},{\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"reasoning\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"We are given an issue: \\\\\\\"дробовик и наступательная граната должен открываться при прохождении карты Здание на любой ранг (даже на F)\\\\\\\"\\\\nTranslation: \\\\\\\"Shotgun and offensive grenade should be unlocked when passing the Building map on any rank (even F)\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nWe need to find where the unlocks for shotgun and offensive grenade are handled, and adjust the condition so that they are unlocked when the Building level is completed, regardless of rank.\\\\n\\\\nFrom the file list, we see:\\\\n- ./scripts/levels/building_level.gd\\\\n- ./scripts/ui/unlock_table_menu.gd\\\\n\\\\nWe should look at the building level script to see if it has any unlock logic, and also check the unlock table menu.\\\\n\\\\nLet's first examine the building level script.\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool-call\\\",\\\"toolCallId\\\":\\\"chatcmpl-tool-8be0d13d8fb755ef\\\",\\\"toolName\\\":\\\"read\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1776272033963/scripts/levels/building_level.gd\\\"}}]},{\\\"role\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool-result\\\",\\\"toolCallId\\\":\\\"chatcmpl-tool-8be0d13d8fb755ef\\\",\\\"toolName\\\":\\\"read\\\",\\\"output\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"<file>\\\\n00001| extends Node2D\\\\n00002| ## Building level scene for the Godot Top-Down Template.\\\\n00003| ##\\\\n00004| ## This scene is a Hotline Miami 2 style building with rooms and halls.\\\\n00005| ## Features:\\\\n00006| ## - Building interior layout (~2400x2000 pixels) larger than viewport\\\\n00007| ## - Multiple interconnected rooms with corridors\\\\n00008| ## - 10 enemies distributed across different rooms (2+ per room)\\\\n00009| ## - Clear room boundaries with walls and doorways\\\\n00010| ## - Similar mechanics to TestTier (ammo tracking, enemy tracking, etc.)\\\\n00011| ## - Score tracking with Hotline Miami style ranking system\\\\n00012| ## - Dim window moonlight in corridors without enemies for night mode visibility (Issue #593)\\\\n00013| \\\\n00014| ## Reference to the enemy count label.\\\\n00015| var _enemy_count_label: Label = null\\\\n00016| \\\\n00017| ## Reference to the ammo count label.\\\\n00018| var _ammo_label: Label = null\\\\n00019| \\\\n00020| ## Reference to the player.\\\\n00021| var _player: Node2D = null\\\\n00022| \\\\n00023| ## Total enemy count at start.\\\\n00024| var _initial_enemy_count: int = 0\\\\n00025| \\\\n00026| ## Current enemy count.\\\\n00027| var _current_enemy_count: int = 0\\\\n00028| \\\\n00029| ## Whether game over has been shown.\\\\n00030| var _game_over_shown: bool = false\\\\n00031| \\\\n00032| ## Reference to the difficulty label.\\\\n00033| var _difficulty_label: Label = null\\\\n00034| \\\\n00035| ## Reference to the magazines label (shows individual magazine ammo counts).\\\\n00036| var _magazines_label: Label = null\\\\n00037| \\\\n00038| ## Reference to the ColorRect for saturation effect.\\\\n00039| var _saturation_overlay: ColorRect = null\\\\n00040| \\\\n00041| ## Reference to the combo label.\\\\n00042| var _combo_label: Label = null\\\\n00043| ## Reference to active combo tween (to cancel if needed).\\\\n00044| var _combo_tween: Tween = null\\\\n00045| \\\\n00046| ## Reference to the exit zone.\\\\n00047| var _exit_zone: Area2D = null\\\\n00048| \\\\n00049| ## Whether the level has been cleared (all enemies eliminated).\\\\n00050| var _level_cleared: bool = false\\\\n00051| \\\\n00052| ## Whether the score screen is currently shown (for W key shortcut).\\\\n00053| var _score_shown: bool = false\\\\n00054| \\\\n00055| ## Whether the level completion sequence has been triggered (prevents duplicate calls).\\\\n00056| var _level_completed: bool = false\\\\n00057| \\\\n00058| ## Duration of saturation effect in seconds.\\\\n00059| const SATURATION_DURATION: float = 0.15\\\\n00060| \\\\n00061| ## Saturation effect intensity (alpha).\\\\n00062| const SATURATION_INTENSITY: float = 0.25\\\\n00063| \\\\n00064| ## List of enemy nodes for position tracking.\\\\n00065| var _enemies: Array = []\\\\n00066| \\\\n00067| ## Cached reference to the ReplayManager autoload (C# singleton).\\\\n00068| var _replay_manager: Node = null\\\\n00069| \\\\n00070| ## Weapon hints component instance (Issue #809).\\\\n00071| var _weapon_hints_component: Node = null\\\\n00072| \\\\n00073| ## Whether debug mode (F7) is active — controls passage waypoint visualization (#1226).\\\\n00074| var _debug_mode: bool = false\\\\n00075| \\\\n00076| \\\\n00077| ## Gets the ReplayManager autoload node.\\\\n00078| ## The ReplayManager is now a C# autoload that works reliably in exported builds,\\\\n00079| ## replacing the GDScript version that had Godot 4.3 binary tokenization issues\\\\n00080| ## (godotengine/godot#94150, godotengine/godot#96065).\\\\n00081| func _get_or_create_replay_manager() -> Node:\\\\n00082| \\\\tif _replay_manager != null and is_instance_valid(_replay_manager):\\\\n00083| \\\\t\\\\treturn _replay_manager\\\\n00084| \\\\n00085| \\\\t_replay_manager = get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"/root/ReplayManager\\\\\\\")\\\\n00086| \\\\tif _replay_manager != null:\\\\n00087| \\\\t\\\\t# C# methods must be called with PascalCase from GDScript (no auto-conversion for user methods)\\\\n00088| \\\\t\\\\tif _replay_manager.has_method(\\\\\\\"StartRecording\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00089| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"ReplayManager found as C# autoload - verified OK\\\\\\\")\\\\n00090| \\\\t\\\\telse:\\\\n00091| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"WARNING: ReplayManager autoload exists but has no StartRecording method\\\\\\\")\\\\n00092| \\\\telse:\\\\n00093| \\\\t\\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"ERROR: ReplayManager autoload not found at /root/ReplayManager\\\\\\\")\\\\n00094| \\\\n00095| \\\\treturn _replay_manager\\\\n00096| \\\\n00097| \\\\n00098| func _ready() -> void:\\\\n00099| \\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"BuildingLevel loaded - Hotline Miami Style\\\\\\\")\\\\n00100| \\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"Building size: ~2400x2000 pixels\\\\\\\")\\\\n00101| \\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"Clear all rooms to win!\\\\\\\")\\\\n00102| \\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"Press Q for quick restart\\\\\\\")\\\\n00103| \\\\n00104| \\\\t# Setup navigation mesh for enemy pathfinding\\\\n00105| \\\\t_setup_navigation()\\\\n00106| \\\\n00107| \\\\t# Find and connect to all enemies\\\\n00108| \\\\t_setup_enemy_tracking()\\\\n00109| \\\\n00110| \\\\t# Find the enemy count label\\\\n00111| \\\\t_enemy_count_label = get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"CanvasLayer/UI/EnemyCountLabel\\\\\\\")\\\\n00112| \\\\t_update_enemy_count_label()\\\\n00113| \\\\n00114| \\\\t# Find and setup player tracking\\\\n00115| \\\\t_setup_player_tracking()\\\\n00116| \\\\n00117| \\\\t# Restrict camera so the border walls are never visible (Issue #1682).\\\\n00118| \\\\t_configure_camera()\\\\n00119| \\\\n00120| \\\\t# Setup debug UI\\\\n00121| \\\\t_setup_debug_ui()\\\\n00122| \\\\n00123| \\\\t# Setup saturation overlay for kill effect\\\\n00124| \\\\t_setup_saturation_overlay()\\\\n00125| \\\\n00126| \\\\t# Connect to GameManager signals\\\\n00127| \\\\tif GameManager:\\\\n00128| \\\\t\\\\tGameManager.enemy_killed.connect(_on_game_manager_enemy_killed)\\\\n00129| \\\\t\\\\tGameManager.stats_updated.connect(_update_debug_ui)\\\\n00130| \\\\t\\\\tif GameManager.has_signal(\\\\\\\"debug_mode_toggled\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00131| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tGameManager.debug_mode_toggled.connect(_on_debug_mode_toggled)\\\\n00132| \\\\t\\\\tif GameManager.has_method(\\\\\\\"is_debug_mode_enabled\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00133| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_debug_mode = GameManager.is_debug_mode_enabled(); if _debug_mode: queue_redraw()\\\\n00134| \\\\n00135| \\\\t# Initialize ScoreManager for this level\\\\n00136| \\\\t_initialize_score_manager()\\\\n00137| \\\\n00138| \\\\t# Setup exit zone near player spawn (left wall)\\\\n00139| \\\\t_setup_exit_zone()\\\\n00140| \\\\n00141| \\\\t# Setup window lights in corridors without enemies (Issue #593)\\\\n00142| \\\\t_setup_window_lights()\\\\n00143| \\\\n00144| \\\\t# Setup warm ceiling lights in the center of large rooms (Issue #1206)\\\\n00145| \\\\t_setup_room_warm_lights()\\\\n00146| \\\\n00147| \\\\t# Start replay recording\\\\n00148| \\\\t_start_replay_recording()\\\\n00149| \\\\n00150| \\\\t# Setup weapon hints (Issue #809)\\\\n00151| \\\\t_setup_weapon_hints()\\\\n00152| \\\\n00153| \\\\n00154| ## Initialize the ScoreManager for this level.\\\\n00155| func _initialize_score_manager() -> void:\\\\n00156| \\\\tvar score_manager: Node = get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"/root/ScoreManager\\\\\\\")\\\\n00157| \\\\tif score_manager == null:\\\\n00158| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00159| \\\\n00160| \\\\t# Start tracking for this level\\\\n00161| \\\\tscore_manager.start_level(_initial_enemy_count)\\\\n00162| \\\\n00163| \\\\t# Set player reference\\\\n00164| \\\\tif _player:\\\\n00165| \\\\t\\\\tscore_manager.set_player(_player)\\\\n00166| \\\\n00167| \\\\t# Connect to combo changes for UI feedback\\\\n00168| \\\\tif not score_manager.combo_changed.is_connected(_on_combo_changed):\\\\n00169| \\\\t\\\\tscore_manager.combo_changed.connect(_on_combo_changed)\\\\n00170| \\\\n00171| \\\\n00172| ## Starts recording the replay for this level.\\\\n00173| func _start_replay_recording() -> void:\\\\n00174| \\\\tvar replay_manager: Node = _get_or_create_replay_manager()\\\\n00175| \\\\tif replay_manager == null:\\\\n00176| \\\\t\\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"ERROR: ReplayManager could not be loaded, replay recording disabled\\\\\\\")\\\\n00177| \\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] ERROR: ReplayManager could not be loaded!\\\\\\\")\\\\n00178| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00179| \\\\n00180| \\\\t# Log player and enemies status for debugging\\\\n00181| \\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"Starting replay recording - Player: %s, Enemies count: %d\\\\\\\" % [\\\\n00182| \\\\t\\\\t_player.name if _player else \\\\\\\"NULL\\\\\\\",\\\\n00183| \\\\t\\\\t_enemies.size()\\\\n00184| \\\\t])\\\\n00185| \\\\n00186| \\\\tif _player == null:\\\\n00187| \\\\t\\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"WARNING: Player is null, replay may not record properly\\\\\\\")\\\\n00188| \\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] WARNING: Player is null for replay recording!\\\\\\\")\\\\n00189| \\\\n00190| \\\\tif _enemies.is_empty():\\\\n00191| \\\\t\\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"WARNING: No enemies to track in replay\\\\\\\")\\\\n00192| \\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] WARNING: No enemies registered for replay!\\\\\\\")\\\\n00193| \\\\n00194| \\\\t# Clear any previous replay data\\\\n00195| \\\\tif replay_manager.has_method(\\\\\\\"ClearReplay\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00196| \\\\t\\\\treplay_manager.ClearReplay()\\\\n00197| \\\\t\\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"Previous replay data cleared\\\\\\\")\\\\n00198| \\\\n00199| \\\\t# Start recording with player and enemies\\\\n00200| \\\\tif replay_manager.has_method(\\\\\\\"StartRecording\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00201| \\\\t\\\\treplay_manager.StartRecording(self, _player, _enemies)\\\\n00202| \\\\t\\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"Replay recording started successfully\\\\\\\")\\\\n00203| \\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] Replay recording started with %d enemies\\\\\\\" % _enemies.size())\\\\n00204| \\\\telse:\\\\n00205| \\\\t\\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"ERROR: ReplayManager.StartRecording method not found\\\\\\\")\\\\n00206| \\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] ERROR: StartRecording method not found!\\\\\\\")\\\\n00207| \\\\n00208| \\\\n00209| ## Setup the exit zone near the player spawn point (left wall).\\\\n00210| ## The exit appears after all enemies are eliminated.\\\\n00211| func _setup_exit_zone() -> void:\\\\n00212| \\\\t# Load and instantiate the exit zone\\\\n00213| \\\\tvar exit_zone_scene = load(\\\\\\\"res://scenes/objects/ExitZone.tscn\\\\\\\")\\\\n00214| \\\\tif exit_zone_scene == null:\\\\n00215| \\\\t\\\\tpush_warning(\\\\\\\"ExitZone scene not found - score will show immediately on level clear\\\\\\\")\\\\n00216| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00217| \\\\n00218| \\\\t_exit_zone = exit_zone_scene.instantiate()\\\\n00219| \\\\t# Position exit on the left wall near player spawn (player starts at 450, 1250)\\\\n00220| \\\\t# Place exit at left wall (x=80) at similar y position\\\\n00221| \\\\t_exit_zone.position = Vector2(120, 1250)\\\\n00222| \\\\t_exit_zone.zone_width = 60.0\\\\n00223| \\\\t_exit_zone.zone_height = 100.0\\\\n00224| \\\\n00225| \\\\t# Connect the player reached exit signal\\\\n00226| \\\\t_exit_zone.player_reached_exit.connect(_on_player_reached_exit)\\\\n00227| \\\\n00228| \\\\t# Add to the environment node\\\\n00229| \\\\tvar environment := get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"Environment\\\\\\\")\\\\n00230| \\\\tif environment:\\\\n00231| \\\\t\\\\tenvironment.add_child(_exit_zone)\\\\n00232| \\\\telse:\\\\n00233| \\\\t\\\\tadd_child(_exit_zone)\\\\n00234| \\\\n00235| \\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] Exit zone created at position (120, 1250)\\\\\\\")\\\\n00236| \\\\n00237| \\\\n00238| ## Called when the player reaches the exit zone after clearing the level.\\\\n00239| func _on_player_reached_exit() -> void:\\\\n00240| \\\\tif not _level_cleared:\\\\n00241| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00242| \\\\n00243| \\\\t# Prevent duplicate calls (exit zone can fire multiple times)\\\\n00244| \\\\tif _level_completed:\\\\n00245| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00246| \\\\n00247| \\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] Player reached exit - showing score!\\\\\\\")\\\\n00248| \\\\tcall_deferred(\\\\\\\"_complete_level_with_score\\\\\\\")\\\\n00249| \\\\n00250| \\\\n00251| ## Activate the exit zone after all enemies are eliminated.\\\\n00252| func _activate_exit_zone() -> void:\\\\n00253| \\\\tif _exit_zone and _exit_zone.has_method(\\\\\\\"activate\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00254| \\\\t\\\\t_exit_zone.activate()\\\\n00255| \\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] Exit zone activated - go to exit to see score!\\\\\\\")\\\\n00256| \\\\telse:\\\\n00257| \\\\t\\\\t# Fallback: if exit zone not available, show score immediately\\\\n00258| \\\\t\\\\tpush_warning(\\\\\\\"Exit zone not available - showing score immediately\\\\\\\")\\\\n00259| \\\\t\\\\t_complete_level_with_score()\\\\n00260| \\\\n00261| \\\\n00262| ## Setup realistic visibility for the player (Issue #540).\\\\n00263| ## Adds the RealisticVisibilityComponent to the player node.\\\\n00264| ## The component handles CanvasModulate (darkness) + PointLight2D (player vision)\\\\n00265| ## and reacts to ExperimentalSettings.realistic_visibility_enabled toggle.\\\\n00266| func _setup_realistic_visibility() -> void:\\\\n00267| \\\\tif _player == null:\\\\n00268| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00269| \\\\n00270| \\\\tvar visibility_script = load(\\\\\\\"res://scripts/components/realistic_visibility_component.gd\\\\\\\")\\\\n00271| \\\\tif visibility_script == null:\\\\n00272| \\\\t\\\\tpush_warning(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] RealisticVisibilityComponent script not found\\\\\\\")\\\\n00273| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00274| \\\\n00275| \\\\tvar visibility_component = Node.new()\\\\n00276| \\\\tvisibility_component.name = \\\\\\\"RealisticVisibilityComponent\\\\\\\"\\\\n00277| \\\\tvisibility_component.set_script(visibility_script)\\\\n00278| \\\\t_player.add_child(visibility_component)\\\\n00279| \\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] Realistic visibility component added to player\\\\\\\")\\\\n00280| \\\\n00281| \\\\n00282| ## Setup weapon hints component (Issue #809).\\\\n00283| ## Shows weapon-specific tutorial hints when player uses a new weapon.\\\\n00284| func _setup_weapon_hints() -> void:\\\\n00285| \\\\tif _player == null:\\\\n00286| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00287| \\\\n00288| \\\\tvar canvas_layer: Node = get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"CanvasLayer\\\\\\\")\\\\n00289| \\\\tif canvas_layer == null:\\\\n00290| \\\\t\\\\tpush_warning(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] CanvasLayer node not found for weapon hints\\\\\\\")\\\\n00291| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00292| \\\\n00293| \\\\tvar hints_script = load(\\\\\\\"res://scripts/components/weapon_hints_component.gd\\\\\\\")\\\\n00294| \\\\tif hints_script == null:\\\\n00295| \\\\t\\\\tpush_warning(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] WeaponHintsComponent script not found\\\\\\\")\\\\n00296| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00297| \\\\n00298| \\\\t_weapon_hints_component = Node.new()\\\\n00299| \\\\t_weapon_hints_component.name = \\\\\\\"WeaponHintsComponent\\\\\\\"\\\\n00300| \\\\t_weapon_hints_component.set_script(hints_script)\\\\n00301| \\\\tadd_child(_weapon_hints_component)\\\\n00302| \\\\n00303| \\\\t# Setup the component with player and CanvasLayer references (Issue #809)\\\\n00304| \\\\tif _weapon_hints_component.has_method(\\\\\\\"setup\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00305| \\\\t\\\\t_weapon_hints_component.setup(_player, canvas_layer)\\\\n00306| \\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] Weapon hints component added and setup\\\\\\\")\\\\n00307| \\\\n00308| \\\\n00309| ## Setup warm ceiling lights in the centers of large rooms (Issue #1206).\\\\n00310| ## Adds PointLight2D nodes with warm yellow-orange color to make the rooms\\\\n00311| ## look cozy and aesthetically pleasing.\\\\n00312| ##\\\\n00313| ## ## Light placement rules\\\\n00314| ## 1. Default position: geometric center of the room (average of its bounding box).\\\\n00315| ## 2. If a large obstacle (table, server rack, wall junction, etc.) sits at the\\\\n00316| ##    geometric center, shift the light to the nearest open area — typically\\\\n00317| ##    offset toward the side that has the most free floor space.\\\\n00318| ## 3. If a wall junction or shadow-casting surface is close (< 30 px) to the\\\\n00319| ##    light source, move the light inward until it is fully inside the open\\\\n00320| ##    floor area so shadows don't block the cone.\\\\n00321| ## 4. Prefer the upper half of a room when the lower half is crowded or when\\\\n00322| ##    the room label (\\\\\\\"OFFICE 2\\\\\\\", etc.) already anchors the top edge visually.\\\\n00323| ##\\\\n00324| ## Room centers (derived from RoomLabel bounds in the scene):\\\\n00325| ## - Conference Room: ~(1918, 340)  — geometric center, no obstacles\\\\n00326| ## - Break Room:      ~(1918, 994)  — geometric center, no obstacles\\\\n00327| ## - Server Room:     ~(2200, 1638) — shifted right, away from right-wall junction\\\\n00328| ## - Main Hall:       ~(1200, 1724) — geometric center, no obstacles\\\\n00329| ## - Office 1:        ~(290, 384)   — geometric center, no obstacles\\\\n00330| ## - Office 2:        ~(718, 780)   — shifted up from center (856) to upper half\\\\n00331| func _setup_room_warm_lights() -> void:\\\\n00332| \\\\tvar environment := get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"Environment\\\\\\\")\\\\n00333| \\\\tif environment == null:\\\\n00334| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00335| \\\\n00336| \\\\t# Container node for all room lights\\\\n00337| \\\\tvar room_lights_node := Node2D.new()\\\\n00338| \\\\troom_lights_node.name = \\\\\\\"RoomLights\\\\\\\"\\\\n00339| \\\\tenvironment.add_child(room_lights_node)\\\\n00340| \\\\n00341| \\\\t# Large rooms get prominent warm lights; smaller rooms get subtler ones.\\\\n00342| \\\\t# Format: [position, energy, texture_scale, label]\\\\n00343| \\\\tvar room_configs: Array = [\\\\n00344| \\\\t\\\\t# Large rooms — bigger lights\\\\n00345| \\\\t\\\\t[Vector2(1918, 340),  0.9, 5.0, \\\\\\\"ConferenceRoom\\\\\\\"],\\\\n00346| \\\\t\\\\t[Vector2(1918, 994),  0.9, 5.0, \\\\\\\"BreakRoom\\\\\\\"],\\\\n00347| \\\\t\\\\t[Vector2(2200, 1638), 0.9, 5.0, \\\\\\\"ServerRoom\\\\\\\"],\\\\n00348| \\\\t\\\\t[Vector2(1200, 1724), 0.85, 4.5, \\\\\\\"MainHall\\\\\\\"],\\\\n00349| \\\\t\\\\t# Smaller rooms — softer lights\\\\n00350| \\\\t\\\\t[Vector2(290, 384),   0.7, 3.5, \\\\\\\"Office1\\\\\\\"],\\\\n00351| \\\\t\\\\t# Office 2: shifted to upper half (y=780 instead of centre y=856)\\\\n00352| \\\\t\\\\t# so the glow covers the label zone and the lower-half corridor approach.\\\\n00353| \\\\t\\\\t[Vector2(718, 780),   0.7, 3.5, \\\\\\\"Office2\\\\\\\"],\\\\n00354| \\\\t]\\\\n00355| \\\\n00356| \\\\tfor cfg in room_configs:\\\\n00357| \\\\t\\\\t_create_room_warm_light(room_lights_node, cfg[0], cfg[1], cfg[2], cfg[3])\\\\n00358| \\\\n00359| \\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] Warm ceiling lights placed in all rooms (Issue #1206)\\\\\\\")\\\\n00360| \\\\n00361| \\\\n00362| ## Create a single warm ceiling light at the given room-center position.\\\\n00363| ## Uses a soft radial gradient that fades smoothly to black, producing a natural\\\\n00364| ## \\\\\\\"overhead lamp\\\\\\\" feel with no hard visible edge.\\\\n00365| ## @param parent: Container node.\\\\n00366| ## @param pos: World-space position (room center).\\\\n00367| ## @param energy: Light brightness (0–1 range, typical 0.7–0.9).\\\\n00368| ## @param scale: Texture scale controlling the light radius.\\\\n00369| ## @param room_name: Name suffix for the node (debug convenience).\\\\n00370| func _create_room_warm_light(parent: Node2D, pos: Vector2, energy: float, scale: float, room_name: String) -> void:\\\\n00371| \\\\tvar light_node := Node2D.new()\\\\n00372| \\\\tlight_node.name = \\\\\\\"WarmLight_%s\\\\\\\" % room_name\\\\n00373| \\\\tlight_node.position = pos\\\\n00374| \\\\tparent.add_child(light_node)\\\\n00375| \\\\n00376| \\\\t# Small visual indicator — a dim warm-colored circle representing the lamp fixture.\\\\n00377| \\\\t# Uses Sprite2D (not Control/ColorRect) so it does NOT intercept mouse events and\\\\n00378| \\\\t# cannot break pause-menu or UI clicks.\\\\n00379| \\\\tvar fixture := Sprite2D.new()\\\\n00380| \\\\tfixture.name = \\\\\\\"Fixture\\\\\\\"\\\\n00381| \\\\tfixture.texture = _create_lamp_fixture_texture()\\\\n00382| \\\\tfixture.modulate = Color(1.0, 0.85, 0.5, 0.5)  # Pale warm amber, semi-transparent\\\\n00383| \\\\tlight_node.add_child(fixture)\\\\n00384| \\\\n00385| \\\\t# The actual PointLight2D\\\\n00386| \\\\tvar light := PointLight2D.new()\\\\n00387| \\\\tlight.name = \\\\\\\"PointLight\\\\\\\"\\\\n00388| \\\\tlight.color = Color(1.0, 0.75, 0.3, 1.0)   # Warm amber-orange\\\\n00389| \\\\tlight.energy = energy\\\\n00390| \\\\tlight.shadow_enabled = true\\\\n00391| \\\\tlight.shadow_filter = PointLight2D.SHADOW_FILTER_PCF5\\\\n00392| \\\\tlight.shadow_filter_smooth = 4.0  # Soft shadow edges\\\\n00393| \\\\tlight.texture = _create_warm_light_texture()\\\\n00394| \\\\tlight.texture_scale = scale\\\\n00395| \\\\tlight_node.add_child(light)\\\\n00396| \\\\n00397| \\\\n00398| ## Create a soft radial gradient texture for the warm room lights.\\\\n00399| ## Uses a smooth natural falloff (bright core → gentle taper → complete black).\\\\n00400| ## No abrupt cutoff — the light fades organically like a real overhead lamp.\\\\n00401| func _create_warm_light_texture() -> ImageTexture:\\\\n00402| \\\\tvar size := 512\\\\n00403| \\\\tvar center := Vector2(size * 0.5, size * 0.5)\\\\n00404| \\\\tvar outer_r := size * 0.5  # 256 px\\\\n00405| \\\\n00406| \\\\tvar image := Image.create(size, size, false, Image.FORMAT_RGBA8)\\\\n00407| \\\\n00408| \\\\tfor y in range(size):\\\\n00409| \\\\t\\\\tfor x in range(size):\\\\n00410| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar dist := Vector2(x, y).distance_to(center)\\\\n00411| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar t := clampf(dist / outer_r, 0.0, 1.0)  # 0 = center, 1 = edge\\\\n00412| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t# Smooth inverse-square-ish falloff using a cosine curve:\\\\n00413| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t# bright centre → smooth mid-field → natural fade at rim\\\\n00414| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar brightness := pow(1.0 - t, 2.2)\\\\n00415| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\timage.set_pixel(x, y, Color(brightness, brightness, brightness, 1.0))\\\\n00416| \\\\n00417| \\\\treturn ImageTexture.create_from_image(image)\\\\n00418| \\\\n00419| \\\\n00420| ## Create a small circular texture for the lamp fixture visual indicator.\\\\n00421| ## Returns a soft-edged disc so the fixture looks like a round ceiling lamp,\\\\n00422| ## not a square. Drawn with per-pixel math so the disc has smooth anti-aliased edges.\\\\n00423| func _create_lamp_fixture_texture() -> ImageTexture:\\\\n00424| \\\\tvar size := 32\\\\n00425| \\\\tvar center := Vector2(size * 0.5, size * 0.5)\\\\n00426| \\\\tvar outer_r := size * 0.5  # full disc radius\\\\n00427| \\\\n00428| \\\\tvar image := Image.create(size, size, false, Image.FORMAT_RGBA8)\\\\n00429| \\\\n00430| \\\\tfor y in range(size):\\\\n00431| \\\\t\\\\tfor x in range(size):\\\\n00432| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar dist := Vector2(x, y).distance_to(center)\\\\n00433| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tif dist >= outer_r:\\\\n00434| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\timage.set_pixel(x, y, Color(0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0))\\\\n00435| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\telse:\\\\n00436| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t# Full brightness in the core, soft fade toward the rim\\\\n00437| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar t := clampf(dist / outer_r, 0.0, 1.0)\\\\n00438| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar alpha := pow(1.0 - t, 1.5)\\\\n00439| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\timage.set_pixel(x, y, Color(1.0, 1.0, 1.0, alpha))\\\\n00440| \\\\n00441| \\\\treturn ImageTexture.create_from_image(image)\\\\n00442| \\\\n00443| \\\\n00444| ## Setup window lights in corridors and rooms without enemies (Issue #593).\\\\n00445| ## Places dim blue PointLight2D nodes along exterior walls to simulate moonlight\\\\n00446| ## coming through windows. Only in areas without enemies so dark rooms with enemies\\\\n00447| ## remain tense and challenging.\\\\n00448| ## Window visuals (small blue ColorRect) are placed on the wall surface.\\\\n00449| ##\\\\n00450| ## Lighting architecture:\\\\n00451| ## - Each window has ONE primary PointLight2D (low energy, shadows on) for the\\\\n00452| ##   visible moonlight patch near the window.\\\\n00453| ## - ONE DirectionalLight2D provides scene-wide ambient moonlight glow with\\\\n00454| ##   NO visible edges. DirectionalLight2D illuminates the entire scene uniformly\\\\n00455| ##   (unlike PointLight2D which has a finite circular boundary).\\\\n00456| func _setup_window_lights() -> void:\\\\n00457| \\\\tvar environment := get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"Environment\\\\\\\")\\\\n00458| \\\\tif environment == null:\\\\n00459| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00460| \\\\n00461| \\\\t# Create a container node for all window lights\\\\n00462| \\\\tvar windows_node := Node2D.new()\\\\n00463| \\\\twindows_node.name = \\\\\\\"WindowLights\\\\\\\"\\\\n00464| \\\\tenvironment.add_child(windows_node)\\\\n00465| \\\\n00466| \\\\t# Window light positions: [position, wall_side]\\\\n00467| \\\\t# wall_side: \\\\\\\"top\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"bottom\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"left\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"right\\\\\\\" determines window visual orientation\\\\n00468| \\\\t# Placed ONLY in corridors/rooms WITHOUT enemies:\\\\n00469| \\\\t# - Central corridor (x=512-1376, y=700-1012)\\\\n00470| \\\\t# - Left lobby area (x=64-900, y=1000-1400)\\\\n00471| \\\\t# - Storage room (x=80-500, y=1612-2048)\\\\n00472| \\\\n00473| \\\\t# Left wall windows (x=64) - lobby and storage areas (no enemies)\\\\n00474| \\\\t_create_window_light(windows_node, Vector2(64, 1100), \\\\\\\"left\\\\\\\")\\\\n00475| \\\\t_create_window_light(windows_node, Vector2(64, 1250), \\\\\\\"left\\\\\\\")\\\\n00476| \\\\t_create_window_light(windows_node, Vector2(64, 1750), \\\\\\\"left\\\\\\\")\\\\n00477| \\\\t_create_window_light(windows_node, Vector2(64, 1900), \\\\\\\"left\\\\\\\")\\\\n00478| \\\\n00479| \\\\t# Top wall windows (y=64) - above corridor area (no enemies in corridor)\\\\n00480| \\\\t_create_window_light(windows_node, Vector2(700, 64), \\\\\\\"top\\\\\\\")\\\\n00481| \\\\t_create_window_light(windows_node, Vector2(900, 64), \\\\\\\"top\\\\\\\")\\\\n00482| \\\\t_create_window_light(windows_node, Vector2(1100, 64), \\\\\\\"top\\\\\\\")\\\\n00483| \\\\n00484| \\\\t# Bottom wall windows (y=2064) - below storage and lobby (no enemies)\\\\n00485| \\\\t_create_window_light(windows_node, Vector2(200, 2064), \\\\\\\"bottom\\\\\\\")\\\\n00486| \\\\t_create_window_light(windows_node, Vector2(400, 2064), \\\\\\\"bottom\\\\\\\")\\\\n00487| \\\\t_create_window_light(windows_node, Vector2(700, 2064), \\\\\\\"bottom\\\\\\\")\\\\n00488| \\\\t_create_window_light(windows_node, Vector2(1100, 2064), \\\\\\\"bottom\\\\\\\")\\\\n00489| \\\\n00490| \\\\t# Scene-wide ambient moonlight using DirectionalLight2D.\\\\n00491| \\\\t# DirectionalLight2D illuminates the entire scene uniformly with NO visible\\\\n00492| \\\\t# edges (unlike PointLight2D which has a finite circular boundary).\\\\n00493| \\\\t# Energy is very low (0.06) so it provides visible wall outlines\\\\n00494| \\\\t# without washing out the scene or hiding weapon muzzle flashes.\\\\n00495| \\\\t_create_ambient_moonlight(windows_node)\\\\n00496| \\\\n00497| \\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] Window lights placed in corridors without enemies (Issue #593)\\\\\\\")\\\\n00498| \\\\n00499| \\\\n00500| ## Create a single window light source at the given position on a wall.\\\\n00501| ## Creates ONE PointLight2D with shadows enabled — the visible moonlight patch\\\\n00502| ## near the window. Shadows from interior walls give the light a natural shape\\\\n00503| ## that respects the building's geometry.\\\\n00504| ## The scene-wide ambient glow is handled separately by _create_ambient_moonlight().\\\\n00505| ##\\\\n00506| ## Light gradient uses an early-fadeout design: the radial gradient reaches\\\\n00507| ## absolute zero at 55% of the radius, leaving 45% of the texture as pure black\\\\n00508| ## buffer. This ensures NO visible edges even against the near-black CanvasModulate.\\\\n00509| ## Combined with large texture_scale (6.0) and low energy (0.12), the light\\\\n00510| ## dissipates naturally with no perceptible boundary.\\\\n00511| ## @param parent: Parent node to add the window to.\\\\n00512| ## @param pos: Position of the window on the wall.\\\\n00513| ## @param wall_side: Which wall the window is on (\\\\\\\"top\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"bottom\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"left\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"right\\\\\\\").\\\\n00514| func _create_window_light(parent: Node2D, pos: Vector2, wall_side: String) -> void:\\\\n00515| \\\\tvar window_node := Node2D.new()\\\\n00516| \\\\twindow_node.name = \\\\\\\"Window_%s_%d_%d\\\\\\\" % [wall_side, int(pos.x), int(pos.y)]\\\\n00517| \\\\twindow_node.position = pos\\\\n00518| \\\\tparent.add_child(window_node)\\\\n00519| \\\\n00520| \\\\t# Create window visual (small blue rectangle on the wall)\\\\n00521| \\\\tvar window_rect := ColorRect.new()\\\\n00522| \\\\twindow_rect.color = Color(0.3, 0.4, 0.7, 0.6)  # Semi-transparent blue\\\\n00523| \\\\t# Size and offset depend on wall orientation\\\\n00524| \\\\tmatch wall_side:\\\\n00525| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\"left\\\\\\\":\\\\n00526| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\twindow_rect.offset_left = -4.0\\\\n00527| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\twindow_rect.offset_top = -20.0\\\\n00528| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\twindow_rect.offset_right = 4.0\\\\n00529| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\twindow_rect.offset_bottom = 20.0\\\\n00530| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\"right\\\\\\\":\\\\n00531| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\twindow_rect.offset_left = -4.0\\\\n00532| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\twindow_rect.offset_top = -20.0\\\\n00533| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\twindow_rect.offset_right = 4.0\\\\n00534| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\twindow_rect.offset_bottom = 20.0\\\\n00535| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\"top\\\\\\\":\\\\n00536| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\twindow_rect.offset_left = -20.0\\\\n00537| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\twindow_rect.offset_top = -4.0\\\\n00538| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\twindow_rect.offset_right = 20.0\\\\n00539| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\twindow_rect.offset_bottom = 4.0\\\\n00540| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\"bottom\\\\\\\":\\\\n00541| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\twindow_rect.offset_left = -20.0\\\\n00542| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\twindow_rect.offset_top = -4.0\\\\n00543| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\twindow_rect.offset_right = 20.0\\\\n00544| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\twindow_rect.offset_bottom = 4.0\\\\n00545| \\\\twindow_node.add_child(window_rect)\\\\n00546| \\\\n00547| \\\\t# --- Primary moonlight (visible patch near the window) ---\\\\n00548| \\\\tvar light := PointLight2D.new()\\\\n00549| \\\\tlight.name = \\\\\\\"MoonLight\\\\\\\"\\\\n00550| \\\\tlight.color = Color(0.4, 0.5, 0.9, 1.0)  # Cool blue moonlight\\\\n00551| \\\\tlight.energy = 0.12  # Low — slightly brighter (Issue #642), large texture_scale compensates for coverage\\\\n00552| \\\\t# Shadows enabled so interior walls cast natural shadows from the moonlight\\\\n00553| \\\\tlight.shadow_enabled = true\\\\n00554| \\\\tlight.shadow_filter = PointLight2D.SHADOW_FILTER_PCF5\\\\n00555| \\\\tlight.shadow_filter_smooth = 4.0  # Higher smoothing for softer shadow edges\\\\n00556| \\\\tlight.shadow_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 0.7)\\\\n00557| \\\\tlight.texture = _create_window_light_texture()\\\\n00558| \\\\tlight.texture_scale = 6.0  # Large scale so gradient fades out well before the edge\\\\n00559| \\\\t# Offset the light inward from the wall so it illuminates the interior\\\\n00560| \\\\tmatch wall_side:\\\\n00561| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\"left\\\\\\\":\\\\n00562| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tlight.position = Vector2(60, 0)\\\\n00563| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\"right\\\\\\\":\\\\n00564| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tlight.position = Vector2(-60, 0)\\\\n00565| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\"top\\\\\\\":\\\\n00566| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tlight.position = Vector2(0, 60)\\\\n00567| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\"bottom\\\\\\\":\\\\n00568| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tlight.position = Vector2(0, -60)\\\\n00569| \\\\twindow_node.add_child(light)\\\\n00570| \\\\n00571| \\\\n00572| ## Create a radial gradient texture for the primary window moonlight.\\\\n00573| ## Uses an early-fadeout design where the gradient reaches absolute zero at 55%\\\\n00574| ## of the radius, leaving 45% of the texture as pure black buffer zone.\\\\n00575| ## This eliminates visible edges at the PointLight2D quad boundary because the\\\\n00576| ## light contribution is already zero well before the texture boundary.\\\\n00577| ## Against the near-black CanvasModulate (0.02, 0.02, 0.04), even subpixel\\\\n00578| ## differences at the boundary could be visible, so the large buffer is critical.\\\\n00579| func _create_window_light_texture() -> GradientTexture2D:\\\\n00580| \\\\tvar gradient := Gradient.new()\\\\n00581| \\\\t# Bright center core (0-10% radius)\\\\n00582| \\\\tgradient.set_color(0, Color(1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0))\\\\n00583| \\\\t# Smooth falloff begins early\\\\n00584| \\\\tgradient.add_point(0.1, Color(0.7, 0.7, 0.7, 1.0))\\\\n00585| \\\\tgradient.add_point(0.2, Color(0.45, 0.45, 0.45, 1.0))\\\\n00586| \\\\tgradient.add_point(0.3, Color(0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 1.0))\\\\n00587| \\\\tgradient.add_point(0.4, Color(0.1, 0.1, 0.1, 1.0))\\\\n00588| \\\\t# Fade to absolute zero by 55% — remaining 45% is pure black buffer\\\\n00589| \\\\tgradient.add_point(0.5, Color(0.02, 0.02, 0.02, 1.0))\\\\n00590| \\\\tgradient.add_point(0.55, Color(0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0))\\\\n00591| \\\\tgradient.set_color(1, Color(0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0))\\\\n00592| \\\\n00593| \\\\tvar texture := GradientTexture2D.new()\\\\n00594| \\\\ttexture.gradient = gradient\\\\n00595| \\\\ttexture.width = 512\\\\n00596| \\\\ttexture.height = 512\\\\n00597| \\\\ttexture.fill = GradientTexture2D.FILL_RADIAL\\\\n00598| \\\\ttexture.fill_from = Vector2(0.5, 0.5)\\\\n00599| \\\\ttexture.fill_to = Vector2(0.5, 0.0)\\\\n00600| \\\\treturn texture\\\\n00601| \\\\n00602| \\\\n00603| ## Create a scene-wide ambient moonlight using DirectionalLight2D.\\\\n00604| ## DirectionalLight2D illuminates the entire scene uniformly — unlike PointLight2D,\\\\n00605| ## it has no position, no radius, and NO visible edges. This is the correct node\\\\n00606| ## for simulating moonlight (parallel rays from a distant source).\\\\n00607| ## Shadows are disabled so the ambient glow passes through all walls uniformly.\\\\n00608| ## @param parent: Parent node to add the ambient light to.\\\\n00609| func _create_ambient_moonlight(parent: Node2D) -> void:\\\\n00610| \\\\tvar ambient := DirectionalLight2D.new()\\\\n00611| \\\\tambient.name = \\\\\\\"AmbientMoonlight\\\\\\\"\\\\n00612| \\\\tambient.color = Color(0.35, 0.45, 0.85, 1.0)  # Subtle blue moonlight tint\\\\n00613| \\\\tambient.energy = 0.06  # Faint — slightly brighter (Issue #642) for better wall outline visibility\\\\n00614| \\\\tambient.shadow_enabled = false  # Must pass through all walls for uniform glow\\\\n00615| \\\\tparent.add_child(ambient)\\\\n00616| \\\\n00617| \\\\n00618| func _process(_delta: float) -> void:\\\\n00619| \\\\t# Update enemy positions for aggressiveness tracking\\\\n00620| \\\\tvar score_manager: Node = get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"/root/ScoreManager\\\\\\\")\\\\n00621| \\\\tif score_manager and score_manager.has_method(\\\\\\\"update_enemy_positions\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00622| \\\\t\\\\tscore_manager.update_enemy_positions(_enemies)\\\\n00623| \\\\t# Issue #959: Re-check level completion when a retaliating pacifist finishes retaliation.\\\\n00624| \\\\tif _current_enemy_count <= 0 and not _level_cleared and not _has_retaliating_pacifists():\\\\n00625| \\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"All enemies eliminated or pacified! Level cleared!\\\\\\\")\\\\n00626| \\\\t\\\\t_level_cleared = true\\\\n00627| \\\\t\\\\tcall_deferred(\\\\\\\"_activate_exit_zone\\\\\\\")\\\\n00628| \\\\n00629| \\\\n00630| ## Called when combo changes.\\\\n00631| func _on_combo_changed(combo: int, points: int) -> void:\\\\n00632| \\\\tif _combo_label == null:\\\\n00633| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00634| \\\\n00635| \\\\tif combo > 0:\\\\n00636| \\\\t\\\\t_combo_label.text = \\\\\\\"x%d COMBO\\\\\\\\n+%d\\\\\\\" % [combo, points]\\\\n00637| \\\\t\\\\t_combo_label.visible = true\\\\n00638| \\\\t\\\\t# Color changes based on combo count\\\\n00639| \\\\t\\\\tvar combo_color := _get_combo_color(combo)\\\\n00640| \\\\t\\\\t_combo_label.add_theme_color_override(\\\\\\\"font_color\\\\\\\", combo_color)\\\\n00641| \\\\t\\\\t# Combo pop animation: scale bounce + fade in (stays visible until combo resets)\\\\n00642| \\\\t\\\\tif _combo_tween != null and _combo_tween.is_valid():\\\\n00643| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_combo_tween.kill()\\\\n00644| \\\\t\\\\t_combo_label.scale = Vector2(0.7, 0.7)\\\\n00645| \\\\t\\\\t_combo_label.modulate = Color(1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 0.0)\\\\n00646| \\\\t\\\\t_combo_tween = create_tween()\\\\n00647| \\\\t\\\\t_combo_tween.set_parallel(true)\\\\n00648| \\\\t\\\\t_combo_tween.tween_property(_combo_label, \\\\\\\"scale\\\\\\\", Vector2(1.0, 1.0), 0.15).set_trans(Tween.TRANS_BACK).set_ease(Tween.EASE_OUT)\\\\n00649| \\\\t\\\\t_combo_tween.tween_property(_combo_label, \\\\\\\"modulate:a\\\\\\\", 1.0, 0.1)\\\\n00650| \\\\t\\\\t_combo_tween.set_parallel(false)\\\\n00651| \\\\telse:\\\\n00652| \\\\t\\\\tif _combo_tween != null and _combo_tween.is_valid():\\\\n00653| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_combo_tween.kill()\\\\n00654| \\\\t\\\\t_combo_tween = create_tween()\\\\n00655| \\\\t\\\\t_combo_tween.tween_property(_combo_label, \\\\\\\"modulate:a\\\\\\\", 0.0, 0.3)\\\\n00656| \\\\t\\\\t_combo_tween.tween_callback(_combo_label.hide)\\\\n00657| \\\\n00658| \\\\n00659| ## Returns a color based on the current combo count.\\\\n00660| ## Higher combos produce more intense/hotter colors.\\\\n00661| func _get_combo_color(combo: int) -> Color:\\\\n00662| \\\\tif combo >= 10:\\\\n00663| \\\\t\\\\treturn Color(1.0, 0.0, 1.0, 1.0)   # Magenta - extreme combo\\\\n00664| \\\\telif combo >= 7:\\\\n00665| \\\\t\\\\treturn Color(1.0, 0.0, 0.3, 1.0)   # Hot pink\\\\n00666| \\\\telif combo >= 5:\\\\n00667| \\\\t\\\\treturn Color(1.0, 0.1, 0.1, 1.0)   # Bright red\\\\n00668| \\\\telif combo >= 4:\\\\n00669| \\\\t\\\\treturn Color(1.0, 0.2, 0.0, 1.0)   # Red-orange\\\\n00670| \\\\telif combo >= 3:\\\\n00671| \\\\t\\\\treturn Color(1.0, 0.4, 0.0, 1.0)   # Hot orange\\\\n00672| \\\\telif combo >= 2:\\\\n00673| \\\\t\\\\treturn Color(1.0, 0.6, 0.1, 1.0)   # Orange\\\\n00674| \\\\telse:\\\\n00675| \\\\t\\\\treturn Color(1.0, 0.8, 0.2, 1.0)   # Gold (combo 1)\\\\n00676| \\\\n00677| \\\\n00678| ## Clamps the camera so the outer border walls are never visible (Issue #1682, #1684).\\\\n00679| ##\\\\n00680| ## BuildingLevel map: 2528x2128 px playfield framed by 32 px walls (size=Vector2(w,32)).\\\\n00681| ## Wall positions and inner-edge calculations (half-size = 32/2 = 16 px):\\\\n00682| ##   WallTop    (1264,   48), half-h=16  → bottom edge y=48+16=64    → limit_top    = 64\\\\n00683| ##   WallBottom (1264, 2080), half-h=16  → top edge   y=2080-16=2064 → limit_bottom = 2064\\\\n00684| ##   WallLeft   (  48, 1064), half-w=16  → right edge x=48+16=64     → limit_left   = 64\\\\n00685| ##   WallRight  (2480, 1064), half-w=16  → left edge  x=2480-16=2464 → limit_right  = 2464\\\\n00686| func _configure_camera() -> void:\\\\n00687| \\\\tif _player == null:\\\\n00688| \\\\t\\\\tpush_warning(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] _configure_camera: _player is null — camera limits not set\\\\\\\")\\\\n00689| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00690| \\\\tvar camera: Camera2D = _player.get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"Camera2D\\\\\\\")\\\\n00691| \\\\tif camera == null:\\\\n00692| \\\\t\\\\tpush_warning(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] Camera2D not found on player — cannot set camera limits\\\\\\\")\\\\n00693| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00694| \\\\tconst LIMIT_TOP: int    =   64   # WallTop bottom edge    (y=48+16)\\\\n00695| \\\\tconst LIMIT_BOTTOM: int = 2064   # WallBottom top edge    (y=2080-16)\\\\n00696| \\\\tconst LIMIT_LEFT: int   =   64   # WallLeft right edge    (x=48+16)\\\\n00697| \\\\tconst LIMIT_RIGHT: int  = 2464   # WallRight left edge    (x=2480-16)\\\\n00698| \\\\tcamera.limit_top    = LIMIT_TOP\\\\n00699| \\\\tcamera.limit_bottom = LIMIT_BOTTOM\\\\n00700| \\\\tcamera.limit_left   = LIMIT_LEFT\\\\n00701| \\\\tcamera.limit_right  = LIMIT_RIGHT\\\\n00702| \\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] Camera2D limits set — top=%d bottom=%d left=%d right=%d — Issue #1684\\\\\\\" % [\\\\n00703| \\\\t\\\\tLIMIT_TOP, LIMIT_BOTTOM, LIMIT_LEFT, LIMIT_RIGHT\\\\n00704| \\\\t])\\\\n00705| \\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"Camera2D limits set — top=%d bottom=%d left=%d right=%d — Issue #1684\\\\\\\" % [\\\\n00706| \\\\t\\\\tLIMIT_TOP, LIMIT_BOTTOM, LIMIT_LEFT, LIMIT_RIGHT\\\\n00707| \\\\t])\\\\n00708| \\\\n00709| \\\\n00710| ## Setup the navigation mesh for enemy pathfinding.\\\\n00711| ## Bakes the NavigationPolygon using physics collision layer 4 (walls).\\\\n00712| func _setup_navigation() -> void:\\\\n00713| \\\\tvar nav_region: NavigationRegion2D = get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"NavigationRegion2D\\\\\\\")\\\\n00714| \\\\tif nav_region == null:\\\\n00715| \\\\t\\\\tpush_warning(\\\\\\\"NavigationRegion2D not found - enemy pathfinding will be limited\\\\\\\")\\\\n00716| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00717| \\\\tvar nav_poly: NavigationPolygon = nav_region.navigation_polygon\\\\n00718| \\\\tif nav_poly == null:\\\\n00719| \\\\t\\\\tpush_warning(\\\\\\\"NavigationPolygon not found - enemy pathfinding will be limited\\\\\\\")\\\\n00720| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00721| \\\\t# Issue #1289: wait for physics frame so CollisionShape2D nodes are registered\\\\n00722| \\\\t# with PhysicsServer2D before parsing source geometry for navmesh carving.\\\\n00723| \\\\tawait get_tree().physics_frame\\\\n00724| \\\\t# Issue #1289: explicit parse+bake so all wall StaticBody2D nodes are found.\\\\n00725| \\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"Baking navigation mesh...\\\\\\\")\\\\n00726| \\\\tvar source_geometry: NavigationMeshSourceGeometryData2D = NavigationMeshSourceGeometryData2D.new()\\\\n00727| \\\\tNavigationServer2D.parse_source_geometry_data(nav_poly, source_geometry, self)\\\\n00728| \\\\tNavigationServer2D.bake_from_source_geometry_data(nav_poly, source_geometry)\\\\n00729| \\\\t# Issue #1289: push updated polygon back into the NavigationServer's live map.\\\\n00730| \\\\t# Without this reassignment, agents still use the pre-bake (uncarved) navmesh.\\\\n00731| \\\\tnav_region.navigation_polygon = nav_poly\\\\n00732| \\\\tnav_region.emit_signal(\\\\\\\"bake_finished\\\\\\\")\\\\n00733| \\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"Navigation mesh baked successfully\\\\\\\")\\\\n00734| \\\\n00735| \\\\n00736| ## Setup tracking for the player.\\\\n00737| func _setup_player_tracking() -> void:\\\\n00738| \\\\t_player = get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"Entities/Player\\\\\\\")\\\\n00739| \\\\tif _player == null:\\\\n00740| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00741| \\\\n00742| \\\\t# Find the ammo label early so _apply_building_ammo_config can update it (Issue #1259)\\\\n00743| \\\\t_ammo_label = get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"CanvasLayer/UI/AmmoLabel\\\\\\\")\\\\n00744| \\\\n00745| \\\\t# Setup realistic visibility component (Issue #540)\\\\n00746| \\\\t_setup_realistic_visibility()\\\\n00747| \\\\n00748| \\\\t# Setup selected weapon based on GameManager selection\\\\n00749| \\\\t_setup_selected_weapon()\\\\n00750| \\\\n00751| \\\\t# Register player with GameManager\\\\n00752| \\\\tif GameManager:\\\\n00753| \\\\t\\\\tGameManager.set_player(_player)\\\\n00754| \\\\n00755| \\\\t# Connect to player death signal (handles both GDScript \\\\\\\"died\\\\\\\" and C# \\\\\\\"Died\\\\\\\")\\\\n00756| \\\\tif _player.has_signal(\\\\\\\"died\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00757| \\\\t\\\\t_player.died.connect(_on_player_died)\\\\n00758| \\\\telif _player.has_signal(\\\\\\\"Died\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00759| \\\\t\\\\t_player.Died.connect(_on_player_died)\\\\n00760| \\\\n00761| \\\\t# Try to get the player's weapon for C# Player\\\\n00762| \\\\t# First try shotgun (if selected), then Mini UZI, then Silenced Pistol, then assault rifle, then MakarovPM\\\\n00763| \\\\tvar weapon = _player.get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"Shotgun\\\\\\\")\\\\n00764| \\\\tif weapon == null:\\\\n00765| \\\\t\\\\tweapon = _player.get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"MiniUzi\\\\\\\")\\\\n00766| \\\\tif weapon == null:\\\\n00767| \\\\t\\\\tweapon = _player.get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"SilencedPistol\\\\\\\")\\\\n00768| \\\\tif weapon == null:\\\\n00769| \\\\t\\\\tweapon = _player.get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"SniperRifle\\\\\\\")\\\\n00770| \\\\tif weapon == null:\\\\n00771| \\\\t\\\\tweapon = _player.get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"AssaultRifle\\\\\\\")\\\\n00772| \\\\tif weapon == null:\\\\n00773| \\\\t\\\\tweapon = _player.get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"AKGL\\\\\\\")\\\\n00774| \\\\tif weapon == null:\\\\n00775| \\\\t\\\\tweapon = _player.get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"Revolver\\\\\\\")\\\\n00776| \\\\tif weapon == null:\\\\n00777| \\\\t\\\\tweapon = _player.get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"MakarovPM\\\\\\\")\\\\n00778| \\\\tif weapon != null:\\\\n00779| \\\\t\\\\t# C# Player with weapon - connect to weapon signals\\\\n00780| \\\\t\\\\tif weapon.has_signal(\\\\\\\"AmmoChanged\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00781| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tweapon.AmmoChanged.connect(_on_weapon_ammo_changed)\\\\n00782| \\\\t\\\\tif weapon.has_signal(\\\\\\\"MagazinesChanged\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00783| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tweapon.MagazinesChanged.connect(_on_magazines_changed)\\\\n00784| \\\\t\\\\tif weapon.has_signal(\\\\\\\"Fired\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00785| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tweapon.Fired.connect(_on_shot_fired)\\\\n00786| \\\\t\\\\t# Connect to ShellCountChanged for shotgun - updates ammo UI during shell-by-shell reload\\\\n00787| \\\\t\\\\tif weapon.has_signal(\\\\\\\"ShellCountChanged\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00788| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tweapon.ShellCountChanged.connect(_on_shell_count_changed)\\\\n00789| \\\\t\\\\t# Initial ammo display from weapon\\\\n00790| \\\\t\\\\tif weapon.get(\\\\\\\"CurrentAmmo\\\\\\\") != null and weapon.get(\\\\\\\"ReserveAmmo\\\\\\\") != null:\\\\n00791| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_update_ammo_label_magazine(weapon.CurrentAmmo, weapon.ReserveAmmo)\\\\n00792| \\\\t\\\\t# Initial magazine display\\\\n00793| \\\\t\\\\tif weapon.has_method(\\\\\\\"GetMagazineAmmoCounts\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00794| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar mag_counts: Array = weapon.GetMagazineAmmoCounts()\\\\n00795| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_update_magazines_label(mag_counts)\\\\n00796| \\\\t\\\\t# Configure silenced pistol ammo based on enemy count\\\\n00797| \\\\t\\\\t_configure_silenced_pistol_ammo(weapon)\\\\n00798| \\\\t\\\\t# Configure 2.5x ammo for MakarovPM (Issue #636)\\\\n00799| \\\\t\\\\t_configure_makarov_pm_ammo(weapon)\\\\n00800| \\\\telse:\\\\n00801| \\\\t\\\\t# GDScript Player - connect to player signals\\\\n00802| \\\\t\\\\tif _player.has_signal(\\\\\\\"ammo_changed\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00803| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_player.ammo_changed.connect(_on_player_ammo_changed)\\\\n00804| \\\\t\\\\t# Initial ammo display\\\\n00805| \\\\t\\\\tif _player.has_method(\\\\\\\"get_current_ammo\\\\\\\") and _player.has_method(\\\\\\\"get_max_ammo\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00806| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_update_ammo_label(_player.get_current_ammo(), _player.get_max_ammo())\\\\n00807| \\\\n00808| \\\\t# Connect reload/ammo depleted signals for enemy aggression behavior\\\\n00809| \\\\t# These signals are used by BOTH C# and GDScript players to notify enemies\\\\n00810| \\\\t# that the player is vulnerable (reloading or out of ammo)\\\\n00811| \\\\t# C# Player uses PascalCase signal names, GDScript uses snake_case\\\\n00812| \\\\tif _player.has_signal(\\\\\\\"ReloadStarted\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00813| \\\\t\\\\t_player.ReloadStarted.connect(_on_player_reload_started)\\\\n00814| \\\\telif _player.has_signal(\\\\\\\"reload_started\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00815| \\\\t\\\\t_player.reload_started.connect(_on_player_reload_started)\\\\n00816| \\\\n00817| \\\\tif _player.has_signal(\\\\\\\"ReloadCompleted\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00818| \\\\t\\\\t_player.ReloadCompleted.connect(_on_player_reload_completed)\\\\n00819| \\\\telif _player.has_signal(\\\\\\\"reload_completed\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00820| \\\\t\\\\t_player.reload_completed.connect(_on_player_reload_completed)\\\\n00821| \\\\n00822| \\\\tif _player.has_signal(\\\\\\\"AmmoDepleted\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00823| \\\\t\\\\t_player.AmmoDepleted.connect(_on_player_ammo_depleted)\\\\n00824| \\\\telif _player.has_signal(\\\\\\\"ammo_depleted\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00825| \\\\t\\\\t_player.ammo_depleted.connect(_on_player_ammo_depleted)\\\\n00826| \\\\n00827| \\\\n00828| ## Setup tracking for all enemies in the scene.\\\\n00829| func _setup_enemy_tracking() -> void:\\\\n00830| \\\\tvar enemies_node := get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"Environment/Enemies\\\\\\\")\\\\n00831| \\\\tif enemies_node == null:\\\\n00832| \\\\t\\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"ERROR: Environment/Enemies node not found!\\\\\\\")\\\\n00833| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00834| \\\\n00835| \\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"Found Environment/Enemies node with %d children\\\\\\\" % enemies_node.get_child_count())\\\\n00836| \\\\t_enemies.clear()\\\\n00837| \\\\tfor child in enemies_node.get_children():\\\\n00838| \\\\t\\\\tvar has_died_signal := child.has_signal(\\\\\\\"died\\\\\\\")\\\\n00839| \\\\t\\\\tvar script_attached := child.get_script() != null\\\\n00840| \\\\t\\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"Child '%s': script=%s, has_died_signal=%s\\\\\\\" % [c
[2026-04-15T16:54:48.019Z] [INFO] hild.name, script_attached, has_died_signal])\\\\n00841| \\\\t\\\\tif has_died_signal:\\\\n00842| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_enemies.append(child)\\\\n00843| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tchild.died.connect(_on_enemy_died)\\\\n00844| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t# Connect to died_with_info for score tracking if available\\\\n00845| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tif child.has_signal(\\\\\\\"died_with_info\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00846| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tchild.died_with_info.connect(_on_enemy_died_with_info)\\\\n00847| \\\\t\\\\t# Track when enemy is hit for accuracy\\\\n00848| \\\\t\\\\tif child.has_signal(\\\\\\\"hit\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00849| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tchild.hit.connect(_on_enemy_hit)\\\\n00850| \\\\t\\\\t# Issue #959: Connect to pacifist signal - pacifists count as killed for level completion\\\\n00851| \\\\t\\\\tif child.has_signal(\\\\\\\"became_pacifist\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00852| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tchild.became_pacifist.connect(_on_enemy_became_pacifist.bind(child))\\\\n00853| \\\\n00854| \\\\t_initial_enemy_count = _enemies.size()\\\\n00855| \\\\t_current_enemy_count = _initial_enemy_count\\\\n00856| \\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"Enemy tracking complete: %d enemies registered\\\\\\\" % _initial_enemy_count)\\\\n00857| \\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"Tracking %d enemies\\\\\\\" % _initial_enemy_count)\\\\n00858| \\\\n00859| \\\\n00860| ## Configure silenced pistol ammo based on enemy count.\\\\n00861| ## This ensures the pistol has exactly enough bullets for all enemies in the level.\\\\n00862| func _configure_silenced_pistol_ammo(weapon: Node) -> void:\\\\n00863| \\\\t# Check if this is a silenced pistol\\\\n00864| \\\\tif weapon.name != \\\\\\\"SilencedPistol\\\\\\\":\\\\n00865| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00866| \\\\n00867| \\\\t# Call the ConfigureAmmoForEnemyCount method if it exists\\\\n00868| \\\\tif weapon.has_method(\\\\\\\"ConfigureAmmoForEnemyCount\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00869| \\\\t\\\\tvar enemy_count: int = _initial_enemy_count\\\\n00870| \\\\t\\\\tvar ammo_multiplier: int = DifficultyManager.get_ammo_multiplier()\\\\n00871| \\\\t\\\\tif ammo_multiplier > 1:\\\\n00872| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tenemy_count *= ammo_multiplier\\\\n00873| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] Gunslinger/PowerFantasy mode: silenced pistol enemy count multiplied by %dx\\\\\\\" % ammo_multiplier)\\\\n00874| \\\\t\\\\tweapon.ConfigureAmmoForEnemyCount(enemy_count)\\\\n00875| \\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] Configured silenced pistol ammo for %d enemies\\\\\\\" % enemy_count)\\\\n00876| \\\\n00877| \\\\t\\\\t# Update the ammo display after configuration\\\\n00878| \\\\t\\\\tif weapon.get(\\\\\\\"CurrentAmmo\\\\\\\") != null and weapon.get(\\\\\\\"ReserveAmmo\\\\\\\") != null:\\\\n00879| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_update_ammo_label_magazine(weapon.CurrentAmmo, weapon.ReserveAmmo)\\\\n00880| \\\\t\\\\tif weapon.has_method(\\\\\\\"GetMagazineAmmoCounts\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00881| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar mag_counts: Array = weapon.GetMagazineAmmoCounts()\\\\n00882| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_update_magazines_label(mag_counts)\\\\n00883| \\\\n00884| \\\\n00885| ## Configure Makarov PM ammo - 2.5x magazines (Issue #636).\\\\n00886| ## Applies to all difficulty modes including Hard.\\\\n00887| func _configure_makarov_pm_ammo(weapon: Node) -> void:\\\\n00888| \\\\tif weapon == null:\\\\n00889| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00890| \\\\n00891| \\\\tif weapon.name != \\\\\\\"MakarovPM\\\\\\\":\\\\n00892| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00893| \\\\n00894| \\\\tvar starting_magazines: int = 4\\\\n00895| \\\\tif weapon.get(\\\\\\\"StartingMagazineCount\\\\\\\") != null:\\\\n00896| \\\\t\\\\tstarting_magazines = weapon.StartingMagazineCount\\\\n00897| \\\\n00898| \\\\tvar pm_magazines: int = int(round(starting_magazines * 2.5))\\\\n00899| \\\\tvar ammo_multiplier: int = DifficultyManager.get_ammo_multiplier()\\\\n00900| \\\\tif ammo_multiplier > 1:\\\\n00901| \\\\t\\\\tpm_magazines *= ammo_multiplier\\\\n00902| \\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] Gunslinger/PowerFantasy mode: MakarovPM magazines multiplied by %dx\\\\\\\" % ammo_multiplier)\\\\n00903| \\\\n00904| \\\\tif weapon.has_method(\\\\\\\"ReinitializeMagazines\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00905| \\\\t\\\\tweapon.ReinitializeMagazines(pm_magazines, true)\\\\n00906| \\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] 2.5x ammo for MakarovPM: %d magazines (was %d)\\\\\\\" % [pm_magazines, starting_magazines])\\\\n00907| \\\\n00908| \\\\t\\\\t# Re-apply auto-reload magazine size reduction if active (Issue #1105).\\\\n00909| \\\\t\\\\t# ReinitializeMagazines resets magazine size to the original value, overriding\\\\n00910| \\\\t\\\\t# the reduction that Player._Ready() applied for the auto-reload passive item.\\\\n00911| \\\\t\\\\tif _player != null and _player.has_method(\\\\\\\"ApplyAutoReloadAfterLevelAmmoConfig\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00912| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_player.ApplyAutoReloadAfterLevelAmmoConfig()\\\\n00913| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] Re-applied auto-reload magazine reduction after ammo config for makarov_pm\\\\\\\")\\\\n00914| \\\\n00915| \\\\t\\\\tif weapon.get(\\\\\\\"CurrentAmmo\\\\\\\") != null and weapon.get(\\\\\\\"ReserveAmmo\\\\\\\") != null:\\\\n00916| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_update_ammo_label_magazine(weapon.CurrentAmmo, weapon.ReserveAmmo)\\\\n00917| \\\\t\\\\tif weapon.has_method(\\\\\\\"GetMagazineAmmoCounts\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00918| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar mag_counts: Array = weapon.GetMagazineAmmoCounts()\\\\n00919| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_update_magazines_label(mag_counts)\\\\n00920| \\\\n00921| \\\\n00922| ## Apply building-level ammo configuration to weapons already equipped by C# Player (Issue #949).\\\\n00923| ## This is called when C# Player.ApplySelectedWeaponFromGameManager() has already equipped the weapon\\\\n00924| ## but we still need to apply building-specific ammo limits (30+30 for M16/AK instead of 30+90).\\\\n00925| func _apply_building_ammo_config(weapon: Node, weapon_id: String) -> void:\\\\n00926| \\\\tif weapon == null:\\\\n00927| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00928| \\\\n00929| \\\\t# M16 and AK+GL should have 2 magazines (30+30) on Building level (Issue #949)\\\\n00930| \\\\tif weapon_id == \\\\\\\"m16\\\\\\\" or weapon_id == \\\\\\\"ak_gl\\\\\\\":\\\\n00931| \\\\t\\\\tvar base_magazines: int = 2\\\\n00932| \\\\t\\\\tvar difficulty_manager: Node = get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"/root/DifficultyManager\\\\\\\")\\\\n00933| \\\\t\\\\tif difficulty_manager:\\\\n00934| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar ammo_multiplier: int = difficulty_manager.get_ammo_multiplier()\\\\n00935| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tif ammo_multiplier > 1:\\\\n00936| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tbase_magazines *= ammo_multiplier\\\\n00937| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"BuildingLevel: Power Fantasy mode - %s magazines multiplied by %dx\\\\\\\" % [weapon.name, ammo_multiplier])\\\\n00938| \\\\t\\\\tif weapon.has_method(\\\\\\\"ReinitializeMagazines\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00939| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tweapon.ReinitializeMagazines(base_magazines, true)\\\\n00940| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"BuildingLevel: %s magazines reinitialized to %d (C# weapon)\\\\\\\" % [weapon.name, base_magazines])\\\\n00941| \\\\n00942| \\\\t\\\\t# Update ammo display\\\\n00943| \\\\t\\\\tif weapon.get(\\\\\\\"CurrentAmmo\\\\\\\") != null and weapon.get(\\\\\\\"ReserveAmmo\\\\\\\") != null:\\\\n00944| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_update_ammo_label_magazine(weapon.CurrentAmmo, weapon.ReserveAmmo)\\\\n00945| \\\\t\\\\tif weapon.has_method(\\\\\\\"GetMagazineAmmoCounts\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00946| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar mag_counts: Array = weapon.GetMagazineAmmoCounts()\\\\n00947| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_update_magazines_label(mag_counts)\\\\n00948| \\\\n00949| \\\\t# Silenced pistol: configure ammo for enemy count\\\\n00950| \\\\telif weapon_id == \\\\\\\"silenced_pistol\\\\\\\":\\\\n00951| \\\\t\\\\t_configure_silenced_pistol_ammo(weapon)\\\\n00952| \\\\n00953| \\\\t# Mini UZI: should also have reduced magazines\\\\n00954| \\\\telif weapon_id == \\\\\\\"mini_uzi\\\\\\\":\\\\n00955| \\\\t\\\\tvar base_magazines: int = 2\\\\n00956| \\\\t\\\\tvar difficulty_manager: Node = get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"/root/DifficultyManager\\\\\\\")\\\\n00957| \\\\t\\\\tif difficulty_manager:\\\\n00958| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar ammo_multiplier: int = difficulty_manager.get_ammo_multiplier()\\\\n00959| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tif ammo_multiplier > 1:\\\\n00960| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tbase_magazines *= ammo_multiplier\\\\n00961| \\\\t\\\\tif weapon.has_method(\\\\\\\"ReinitializeMagazines\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00962| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tweapon.ReinitializeMagazines(base_magazines, true)\\\\n00963| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"BuildingLevel: MiniUzi magazines reinitialized to %d (C# weapon)\\\\\\\" % base_magazines)\\\\n00964| \\\\n00965| \\\\t# After any ammo reinitialization, reapply auto-reload magazine size reduction\\\\n00966| \\\\t# if the player has the auto-reload passive item active (Issue #1067).\\\\n00967| \\\\t# ReinitializeMagazines resets to full magazine size, overriding the reduction\\\\n00968| \\\\t# that Player._Ready() applied. We must re-reduce after each level ammo setup.\\\\n00969| \\\\tif _player != null and _player.has_method(\\\\\\\"ApplyAutoReloadAfterLevelAmmoConfig\\\\\\\"):\\\\n00970| \\\\t\\\\t_player.ApplyAutoReloadAfterLevelAmmoConfig()\\\\n00971| \\\\t\\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] Re-applied auto-reload magazine reduction after ammo config for %s\\\\\\\" % weapon_id)\\\\n00972| \\\\n00973| \\\\n00974| ## Setup debug UI elements for kills and accuracy.\\\\n00975| func _setup_debug_ui() -> void:\\\\n00976| \\\\tvar ui := get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"CanvasLayer/UI\\\\\\\")\\\\n00977| \\\\tif ui == null:\\\\n00978| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n00979| \\\\n00980| \\\\t# Create difficulty label\\\\n00981| \\\\t_difficulty_label = Label.new()\\\\n00982| \\\\t_difficulty_label.name = \\\\\\\"DifficultyLabel\\\\\\\"\\\\n00983| \\\\t_difficulty_label.text = \\\\\\\"Difficulty: \\\\\\\" + DifficultyManager.get_difficulty_name()\\\\n00984| \\\\t_difficulty_label.set_anchors_preset(Control.PRESET_TOP_LEFT)\\\\n00985| \\\\t_difficulty_label.offset_left = 10\\\\n00986| \\\\t_difficulty_label.offset_top = 80\\\\n00987| \\\\t_difficulty_label.offset_right = 200\\\\n00988| \\\\t_difficulty_label.offset_bottom = 110\\\\n00989| \\\\tui.add_child(_difficulty_label)\\\\n00990| \\\\n00991| \\\\t# Create magazines label (shows individual magazine ammo counts)\\\\n00992| \\\\t_magazines_label = Label.new()\\\\n00993| \\\\t_magazines_label.name = \\\\\\\"MagazinesLabel\\\\\\\"\\\\n00994| \\\\t_magazines_label.text = \\\\\\\"MAGS: -\\\\\\\"\\\\n00995| \\\\t_magazines_label.set_anchors_preset(Control.PRESET_TOP_LEFT)\\\\n00996| \\\\t_magazines_label.offset_left = 10\\\\n00997| \\\\t_magazines_label.offset_top = 115\\\\n00998| \\\\t_magazines_label.offset_right = 400\\\\n00999| \\\\t_magazines_label.offset_bottom = 145\\\\n01000| \\\\tui.add_child(_magazines_label)\\\\n01001| \\\\n01002| \\\\t# Create combo label (shows current combo)\\\\n01003| \\\\t# Positioned below the enemy count label (which ends at offset_bottom = 75)\\\\n01004| \\\\tvar gameplay_settings: Node = get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"/root/GameplaySettings\\\\\\\")\\\\n01005| \\\\tvar combo_size: int = gameplay_settings.get_combo_font_size() if gameplay_settings and gameplay_settings.has_method(\\\\\\\"get_combo_font_size\\\\\\\") else 112\\\\n01006| \\\\t_combo_label = Label.new()\\\\n01007| \\\\t_combo_label.name = \\\\\\\"ComboLabel\\\\\\\"\\\\n01008| \\\\t_combo_label.text = \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n01009| \\\\t_combo_label.horizontal_alignment = HORIZONTAL_ALIGNMENT_RIGHT\\\\n01010| \\\\t_combo_label.set_anchors_preset(Control.PRESET_TOP_WIDE)\\\\n01011| \\\\t_combo_label.offset_left = 10\\\\n01012| \\\\t_combo_label.offset_right = -10\\\\n01013| \\\\t_combo_label.offset_top = 80\\\\n01014| \\\\t_combo_label.offset_bottom = _combo_label.offset_top + combo_size * 2 + 20\\\\n01015| \\\\t_combo_label.add_theme_font_size_override(\\\\\\\"font_size\\\\\\\", combo_size)\\\\n01016| \\\\t_combo_label.add_theme_constant_override(\\\\\\\"line_spacing\\\\\\\", 0)\\\\n01017| \\\\t_combo_label.add_theme_color_override(\\\\\\\"font_color\\\\\\\", Color(1.0, 0.8, 0.2, 1.0))\\\\n01018| \\\\t_combo_label.add_theme_font_override(\\\\\\\"font\\\\\\\", load(\\\\\\\"res://assets/fonts/gothic_bitmap.fnt\\\\\\\"))\\\\n01019| \\\\t_combo_label.clip_contents = true\\\\n01020| \\\\t_combo_label.visible = false\\\\n01021| \\\\tui.add_child(_combo_label)\\\\n01022| \\\\n01023| \\\\n01024| \\\\n01025| ## Setup saturation overlay for kill effect.\\\\n01026| func _setup_saturation_overlay() -> void:\\\\n01027| \\\\tvar canvas_layer := get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"CanvasLayer\\\\\\\")\\\\n01028| \\\\tif canvas_layer == null:\\\\n01029| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n01030| \\\\n01031| \\\\t_saturation_overlay = ColorRect.new()\\\\n01032| \\\\t_saturation_overlay.name = \\\\\\\"SaturationOverlay\\\\\\\"\\\\n01033| \\\\t# Yellow/gold tint for saturation increase effect\\\\n01034| \\\\t_saturation_overlay.color = Color(1.0, 0.9, 0.3, 0.0)\\\\n01035| \\\\t_saturation_overlay.set_anchors_preset(Control.PRESET_FULL_RECT)\\\\n01036| \\\\t_saturation_overlay.mouse_filter = Control.MOUSE_FILTER_IGNORE\\\\n01037| \\\\t# Add to the front\\\\n01038| \\\\tcanvas_layer.add_child(_saturation_overlay)\\\\n01039| \\\\tcanvas_layer.move_child(_saturation_overlay, canvas_layer.get_child_count() - 1)\\\\n01040| \\\\n01041| \\\\n01042| ## Update debug UI with current stats.\\\\n01043| func _update_debug_ui() -> void:\\\\n01044| \\\\tif GameManager == null:\\\\n01045| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n01046| \\\\n01047| \\\\tif _difficulty_label:\\\\n01048| \\\\t\\\\t_difficulty_label.text = \\\\\\\"Difficulty: \\\\\\\" + DifficultyManager.get_difficulty_name()\\\\n01049| \\\\n01050| \\\\n01051| ## Called when an enemy dies.\\\\n01052| func _on_enemy_died() -> void:\\\\n01053| \\\\t_current_enemy_count -= 1\\\\n01054| \\\\t_update_enemy_count_label()\\\\n01055| \\\\n01056| \\\\tif _current_enemy_count <= 0 and not _has_retaliating_pacifists():\\\\n01057| \\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"All enemies eliminated! Building cleared!\\\\\\\")\\\\n01058| \\\\t\\\\t_level_cleared = true\\\\n01059| \\\\t\\\\t# Activate exit zone - score will show when player reaches it\\\\n01060| \\\\t\\\\tcall_deferred(\\\\\\\"_activate_exit_zone\\\\\\\")\\\\n01061| \\\\n01062| \\\\n01063| ## Called when an enemy dies with special kill information.\\\\n01064| func _on_enemy_died_with_info(is_ricochet_kill: bool, is_penetration_kill: bool, is_player_kill: bool = true) -> void:\\\\n01065| \\\\t# Register kill with GameManager (Issue #1196: pass player kill flag to count only player kills).\\\\n01066| \\\\tif GameManager:\\\\n01067| \\\\t\\\\tGameManager.register_kill(is_player_kill, is_penetration_kill)\\\\n01068| \\\\t# Register kill with ScoreManager including special kill info\\\\n01069| \\\\tvar score_manager: Node = get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"/root/ScoreManager\\\\\\\")\\\\n01070| \\\\tif score_manager and score_manager.has_method(\\\\\\\"register_kill\\\\\\\"):\\\\n01071| \\\\t\\\\tscore_manager.register_kill(is_ricochet_kill, is_penetration_kill)\\\\n01072| \\\\n01073| \\\\n01074| ## Issue #959: Called when an enemy becomes a pacifist via loudspeaker.\\\\n01075| ## Pacifists count as \\\\\\\"killed\\\\\\\" for level completion purposes.\\\\n01076| func _on_enemy_became_pacifist(enemy: Node) -> void:\\\\n01077| \\\\t_current_enemy_count -= 1\\\\n01078| \\\\t# Issue #959: Do not count pacifist again when it dies - already counted here\\\\n01079| \\\\tif is_instance_valid(enemy) and enemy.died.is_connected(_on_enemy_died):\\\\n01080| \\\\t\\\\tenemy.died.disconnect(_on_enemy_died)\\\\n01081| \\\\t_update_enemy_count_label()\\\\n01082| \\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"[Building] Enemy became pacifist - counting as eliminated\\\\\\\")\\\\n01083| \\\\tif _current_enemy_count <= 0 and not _has_retaliating_pacifists():\\\\n01084| \\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"All enemies eliminated or pacified! Level cleared!\\\\\\\")\\\\n01085| \\\\t\\\\t_level_cleared = true\\\\n01086| \\\\t\\\\tcall_deferred(\\\\\\\"_activate_exit_zone\\\\\\\")\\\\n01087| \\\\n01088| \\\\n01089| ## Returns true if any enemy is a pacifist who is currently retaliating (attacking the player).\\\\n01090| ## Level should not complete while any enemy is still a threat (Issue #959).\\\\n01091| func _has_retaliating_pacifists() -> bool:\\\\n01092| \\\\tfor enemy in get_tree().get_nodes_in_group(\\\\\\\"enemies\\\\\\\"):\\\\n01093| \\\\t\\\\tif is_instance_valid(enemy) and enemy.has_method(\\\\\\\"is_alive\\\\\\\") and enemy.is_alive():\\\\n01094| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tif enemy.has_method(\\\\\\\"is_retaliating\\\\\\\") and enemy.is_retaliating():\\\\n01095| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\treturn true\\\\n01096| \\\\treturn false\\\\n01097| \\\\n01098| \\\\n01099| ## Complete the level and show the score screen.\\\\n01100| func _complete_level_with_score() -> void:\\\\n01101| \\\\t# Prevent duplicate calls\\\\n01102| \\\\tif _level_completed:\\\\n01103| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n01104| \\\\t_level_completed = true\\\\n01105| \\\\n01106| \\\\t# Disable player controls immediately\\\\n01107| \\\\t_disable_player_controls()\\\\n01108| \\\\n01109| \\\\t# Deactivate exit zone to prevent further triggers\\\\n01110| \\\\tif _exit_zone and _exit_zone.has_method(\\\\\\\"deactivate\\\\\\\"):\\\\n01111| \\\\t\\\\t_exit_zone.deactivate()\\\\n01112| \\\\n01113| \\\\t# Stop replay recording\\\\n01114| \\\\tvar replay_manager: Node = _get_or_create_replay_manager()\\\\n01115| \\\\tif replay_manager:\\\\n01116| \\\\t\\\\tif replay_manager.has_method(\\\\\\\"StopRecording\\\\\\\"):\\\\n01117| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\treplay_manager.StopRecording()\\\\n01118| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"Replay recording stopped\\\\\\\")\\\\n01119| \\\\n01120| \\\\t\\\\t# Log replay status for debugging\\\\n01121| \\\\t\\\\tif replay_manager.has_method(\\\\\\\"HasReplay\\\\\\\"):\\\\n01122| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar has_replay: bool = replay_manager.HasReplay()\\\\n01123| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar duration: float = 0.0\\\\n01124| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tif replay_manager.has_method(\\\\\\\"GetReplayDuration\\\\\\\"):\\\\n01125| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tduration = replay_manager.GetReplayDuration()\\\\n01126| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"Replay status: has_replay=%s, duration=%.2fs\\\\\\\" % [has_replay, duration])\\\\n01127| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] Replay status: has_replay=%s, duration=%.2fs\\\\\\\" % [has_replay, duration])\\\\n01128| \\\\telse:\\\\n01129| \\\\t\\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"ERROR: ReplayManager not found when completing level\\\\\\\")\\\\n01130| \\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"[BuildingLevel] ERROR: ReplayManager not found!\\\\\\\")\\\\n01131| \\\\n01132| \\\\tvar score_manager: Node = get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"/root/ScoreManager\\\\\\\")\\\\n01133| \\\\tif score_manager and score_manager.has_method(\\\\\\\"complete_level\\\\\\\"):\\\\n01134| \\\\t\\\\tvar score_data: Dictionary = score_manager.complete_level()\\\\n01135| \\\\t\\\\t# Notify loudspeaker progression (Issue #959)\\\\n01136| \\\\t\\\\tvar aim: Node = get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"/root/ActiveItemManager\\\\\\\")\\\\n01137| \\\\t\\\\tif aim and aim.has_method(\\\\\\\"notify_level_completed\\\\\\\"):\\\\n01138| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\taim.notify_level_completed(score_data.get(\\\\\\\"kills\\\\\\\", 0) > 0)\\\\n01139| \\\\t\\\\t_show_score_screen(score_data)\\\\n01140| \\\\telse:\\\\n01141| \\\\t\\\\t# Fallback to simple victory message if ScoreManager not available\\\\n01142| \\\\t\\\\t_show_victory_message()\\\\n01143| \\\\n01144| \\\\n01145| ## Called when an enemy is hit (for accuracy tracking).\\\\n01146| func _on_enemy_hit() -> void:\\\\n01147| \\\\tif GameManager:\\\\n01148| \\\\t\\\\tGameManager.register_hit()\\\\n01149| \\\\n01150| \\\\n01151| ## Called when a shot is fired (from C# weapon).\\\\n01152| func _on_shot_fired() -> void:\\\\n01153| \\\\tif GameManager:\\\\n01154| \\\\t\\\\tGameManager.register_shot()\\\\n01155| \\\\n01156| \\\\n01157| ## Called when player ammo changes (GDScript Player).\\\\n01158| func _on_player_ammo_changed(current: int, maximum: int) -> void:\\\\n01159| \\\\t_update_ammo_label(current, maximum)\\\\n01160| \\\\t# Register shot for accuracy tracking\\\\n01161| \\\\tif GameManager:\\\\n01162| \\\\t\\\\tGameManager.register_shot()\\\\n01163| \\\\n01164| \\\\n01165| ## Called when weapon ammo changes (C# Player).\\\\n01166| func _on_weapon_ammo_changed(current_ammo: int, reserve_ammo: int) -> void:\\\\n01167| \\\\t_update_ammo_label_magazine(current_ammo, reserve_ammo)\\\\n01168| \\\\t# Check if completely out of ammo\\\\n01169| \\\\tif current_ammo <= 0 and reserve_ammo <= 0:\\\\n01170| \\\\t\\\\tif _current_enemy_count > 0 and not _game_over_shown:\\\\n01171| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_show_game_over_message()\\\\n01172| \\\\n01173| \\\\n01174| ## Called when magazine inventory changes (C# Player).\\\\n01175| func _on_magazines_changed(magazine_ammo_counts: Array) -> void:\\\\n01176| \\\\t_update_magazines_label(magazine_ammo_counts)\\\\n01177| \\\\n01178| \\\\n01179| ## Called when shotgun shell count changes (during shell-by-shell reload).\\\\n01180| ## This allows the ammo counter to update immediately as each shell is loaded.\\\\n01181| func _on_shell_count_changed(shell_count: int, capacity: int) -> void:\\\\n01182| \\\\t# Get the reserve ammo from the weapon for display\\\\n01183| \\\\tvar reserve_ammo: int = 0\\\\n01184| \\\\tif _player:\\\\n01185| \\\\t\\\\tvar weapon = _player.get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"Shotgun\\\\\\\")\\\\n01186| \\\\t\\\\tif weapon != null and weapon.get(\\\\\\\"ReserveAmmo\\\\\\\") != null:\\\\n01187| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\treserve_ammo = weapon.ReserveAmmo\\\\n01188| \\\\t_update_ammo_label_magazine(shell_count, reserve_ammo)\\\\n01189| \\\\n01190| \\\\n01191| ## Called when player runs out of ammo in current magazine.\\\\n01192| ## This notifies nearby enemies that the player tried to shoot with empty weapon.\\\\n01193| ## Note: This does NOT show game over - the player may still have reserve ammo.\\\\n01194| ## Game over is only shown when BOTH current AND reserve ammo are depleted\\\\n01195| ## (handled in _on_weapon_ammo_changed for C# player, or when GDScript player\\\\n01196| ## truly has no ammo left).\\\\n01197| func _on_player_ammo_depleted() -> void:\\\\n01198| \\\\t# Issue #1261: Do NOT broadcast ammo-empty to all enemies globally — that bypasses the\\\\n01199| \\\\t# sound range system and lets out-of-earshot enemies react to the empty click.\\\\n01200| \\\\t# The EMPTY_CLICK sound emitted below already sets player_ammo_empty on enemies within range.\\\\n01201| \\\\tif _player:\\\\n01202| \\\\t\\\\tvar sound_propagation: Node = get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"/root/SoundPropagation\\\\\\\")\\\\n01203| \\\\t\\\\tif sound_propagation and sound_propagation.has_method(\\\\\\\"emit_player_empty_click\\\\\\\"):\\\\n01204| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tsound_propagation.emit_player_empty_click(_player.global_position, _player)\\\\n01205| \\\\n01206| \\\\t# For GDScript player, check if truly out of all ammo (no reserve)\\\\n01207| \\\\t# For C# player, game over is handled in _on_weapon_ammo_changed\\\\n01208| \\\\tif _player and _player.has_method(\\\\\\\"get_current_ammo\\\\\\\"):\\\\n01209| \\\\t\\\\t# GDScript player - max_ammo is the only ammo they have\\\\n01210| \\\\t\\\\tvar current_ammo: int = _player.get_current_ammo()\\\\n01211| \\\\t\\\\tif current_ammo <= 0 and _current_enemy_count > 0 and not _game_over_shown:\\\\n01212| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_show_game_over_message()\\\\n01213| \\\\t# C# player game over is handled via _on_weapon_ammo_changed signal\\\\n01214| \\\\n01215| \\\\n01216| ## Called when player starts reloading.\\\\n01217| ## Notifies nearby enemies that player is vulnerable via sound propagation.\\\\n01218| ## The reload sound can be heard through walls at greater distance than line of sight.\\\\n01219| func _on_player_reload_started() -> void:\\\\n01220| \\\\t_broadcast_player_reloading(true)\\\\n01221| \\\\t# Emit reload sound via SoundPropagation system so enemies can hear through walls\\\\n01222| \\\\tif _player:\\\\n01223| \\\\t\\\\tvar sound_propagation: Node = get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"/root/SoundPropagation\\\\\\\")\\\\n01224| \\\\t\\\\tif sound_propagation and sound_propagation.has_method(\\\\\\\"emit_player_reload\\\\\\\"):\\\\n01225| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tsound_propagation.emit_player_reload(_player.global_position, _player)\\\\n01226| \\\\n01227| \\\\n01228| ## Called when player finishes reloading.\\\\n01229| ## Clears the reloading state for all enemies.\\\\n01230| func _on_player_reload_completed() -> void:\\\\n01231| \\\\t_broadcast_player_reloading(false)\\\\n01232| \\\\t# Also clear ammo empty state since player now has ammo\\\\n01233| \\\\t_broadcast_player_ammo_empty(false)\\\\n01234| \\\\n01235| \\\\n01236| ## Broadcast player reloading state to all enemies.\\\\n01237| func _broadcast_player_reloading(is_reloading: bool) -> void:\\\\n01238| \\\\tvar enemies_node := get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"Environment/Enemies\\\\\\\")\\\\n01239| \\\\tif enemies_node == null:\\\\n01240| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n01241| \\\\n01242| \\\\tfor enemy in enemies_node.get_children():\\\\n01243| \\\\t\\\\tif enemy.has_method(\\\\\\\"set_player_reloading\\\\\\\"):\\\\n01244| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tenemy.set_player_reloading(is_reloading)\\\\n01245| \\\\n01246| \\\\n01247| ## Broadcast player ammo empty state to all enemies.\\\\n01248| func _broadcast_player_ammo_empty(is_empty: bool) -> void:\\\\n01249| \\\\tvar enemies_node := get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"Environment/Enemies\\\\\\\")\\\\n01250| \\\\tif enemies_node == null:\\\\n01251| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n01252| \\\\n01253| \\\\tfor enemy in enemies_node.get_children():\\\\n01254| \\\\t\\\\tif enemy.has_method(\\\\\\\"set_player_ammo_empty\\\\\\\"):\\\\n01255| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tenemy.set_player_ammo_empty(is_empty)\\\\n01256| \\\\n01257| \\\\n01258| ## Called when player dies.\\\\n01259| func _on_player_died() -> void:\\\\n01260| \\\\t_show_death_message()\\\\n01261| \\\\t# Auto-restart via GameManager\\\\n01262| \\\\tif GameManager:\\\\n01263| \\\\t\\\\t# Small delay to show death message\\\\n01264| \\\\t\\\\tawait get_tree().create_timer(0.5).timeout\\\\n01265| \\\\t\\\\t# Issue #1334: After await, verify this node is still valid (scene may have reloaded)\\\\n01266| \\\\t\\\\tif not is_instance_valid(self):\\\\n01267| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n01268| \\\\t\\\\tGameManager.on_player_death()\\\\n01269| \\\\n01270| \\\\n01271| ## Called when GameManager signals enemy killed (for screen effect).\\\\n01272| func _on_game_manager_enemy_killed() -> void:\\\\n01273| \\\\t_show_saturation_effect()\\\\n01274| \\\\n01275| \\\\n01276| ## Shows the saturation effect when killing an enemy.\\\\n01277| func _show_saturation_effect() -> void:\\\\n01278| \\\\tif _saturation_overlay == null:\\\\n01279| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n01280| \\\\n01281| \\\\t# Create a tween for the saturation effect\\\\n01282| \\\\tvar tween := create_tween()\\\\n01283| \\\\t# Flash in\\\\n01284| \\\\ttween.tween_property(_saturation_overlay, \\\\\\\"color:a\\\\\\\", SATURATION_INTENSITY, SATURATION_DURATION * 0.3)\\\\n01285| \\\\t# Flash out\\\\n01286| \\\\ttween.tween_property(_saturation_overlay, \\\\\\\"color:a\\\\\\\", 0.0, SATURATION_DURATION * 0.7)\\\\n01287| \\\\n01288| \\\\n01289| ## Update the ammo label with color coding (simple format for GDScript Player).\\\\n01290| func _update_ammo_label(current: int, maximum: int) -> void:\\\\n01291| \\\\tif _ammo_label == null:\\\\n01292| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n01293| \\\\n01294| \\\\t_ammo_label.text = \\\\\\\"AMMO: %d/%d\\\\\\\" % [current, maximum]\\\\n01295| \\\\n01296| \\\\t# Color coding: red at <=5, yellow at <=10, white otherwise\\\\n01297| \\\\tif current <= 5:\\\\n01298| \\\\t\\\\t_ammo_label.add_theme_color_override(\\\\\\\"font_color\\\\\\\", Color(1.0, 0.2, 0.2, 1.0))\\\\n01299| \\\\telif current <= 10:\\\\n01300| \\\\t\\\\t_ammo_label.add_theme_color_override(\\\\\\\"font_color\\\\\\\", Color(1.0, 1.0, 0.2, 1.0))\\\\n01301| \\\\telse:\\\\n01302| \\\\t\\\\t_ammo_label.add_theme_color_override(\\\\\\\"font_color\\\\\\\", Color(1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0))\\\\n01303| \\\\n01304| \\\\n01305| ## Update the ammo label with magazine format (for C# Player with weapon).\\\\n01306| ## Shows format: AMMO: magazine/reserve (e.g., \\\\\\\"AMMO: 30/60\\\\\\\")\\\\n01307| func _update_ammo_label_magazine(current_mag: int, reserve: int) -> void:\\\\n01308| \\\\tif _ammo_label == null:\\\\n01309| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n01310| \\\\n01311| \\\\t_ammo_label.text = \\\\\\\"AMMO: %d/%d\\\\\\\" % [current_mag, reserve]\\\\n01312| \\\\n01313| \\\\t# Color coding: red when mag <=5, yellow when mag <=10\\\\n01314| \\\\tif current_mag <= 5:\\\\n01315| \\\\t\\\\t_ammo_label.add_theme_color_override(\\\\\\\"font_color\\\\\\\", Color(1.0, 0.2, 0.2, 1.0))\\\\n01316| \\\\telif current_mag <= 10:\\\\n01317| \\\\t\\\\t_ammo_label.add_theme_color_override(\\\\\\\"font_color\\\\\\\", Color(1.0, 1.0, 0.2, 1.0))\\\\n01318| \\\\telse:\\\\n01319| \\\\t\\\\t_ammo_label.add_theme_color_override(\\\\\\\"font_color\\\\\\\", Color(1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0))\\\\n01320| \\\\n01321| \\\\n01322| ## Update the magazines label showing individual magazine ammo counts.\\\\n01323| ## Shows format: MAGS: [30] | 25 | 10 where [30] is current magazine.\\\\n01324| ## Hidden when a shotgun (tube magazine weapon) is equipped.\\\\n01325| func _update_magazines_label(magazine_ammo_counts: Array) -> void:\\\\n01326| \\\\tif _magazines_label == null:\\\\n01327| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n01328| \\\\n01329| \\\\t# Check if player has a weapon with tube magazine (shotgun)\\\\n01330| \\\\t# If so, hide the magazine label as shotguns don't use detachable magazines\\\\n01331| \\\\tvar weapon = null\\\\n01332| \\\\tif _player:\\\\n01333| \\\\t\\\\tweapon = _player.get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"Shotgun\\\\\\\")\\\\n01334| \\\\t\\\\tif weapon == null:\\\\n01335| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tweapon = _player.get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"AssaultRifle\\\\\\\")\\\\n01336| \\\\t\\\\tif weapon == null:\\\\n01337| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tweapon = _player.get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"AKGL\\\\\\\")\\\\n01338| \\\\t\\\\tif weapon == null:\\\\n01339| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tweapon = _player.get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"MiniUzi\\\\\\\")\\\\n01340| \\\\t\\\\tif weapon == null:\\\\n01341| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tweapon = _player.get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"SilencedPistol\\\\\\\")\\\\n01342| \\\\t\\\\tif weapon == null:\\\\n01343| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tweapon = _player.get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"SniperRifle\\\\\\\")\\\\n01344| \\\\t\\\\tif weapon == null:\\\\n01345| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tweapon = _player.get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"Revolver\\\\\\\")\\\\n01346| \\\\t\\\\tif weapon == null:\\\\n01347| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tweapon = _player.get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"MakarovPM\\\\\\\")\\\\n01348| \\\\n01349| \\\\tif weapon != null and weapon.get(\\\\\\\"UsesTubeMagazine\\\\\\\") == true:\\\\n01350| \\\\t\\\\t# Shotgun equipped - hide magazine display\\\\n01351| \\\\t\\\\t_magazines_label.visible = false\\\\n01352| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n01353| \\\\tif weapon != null and weapon.has_signal(\\\\\\\"CylinderStateChanged\\\\\\\"):\\\\n01354| \\\\t\\\\t_magazines_label.visible = false\\\\n01355| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n01356| \\\\t_magazines_label.visible = true\\\\n01357| \\\\n01358| \\\\tif magazine_ammo_counts.is_empty():\\\\n01359| \\\\t\\\\t_magazines_label.text = \\\\\\\"MAGS: -\\\\\\\"\\\\n01360| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n01361| \\\\n01362| \\\\t# Get magazine capacities to distinguish full vs partial spares\\\\n01363| \\\\tvar mag_max_counts: Array = []\\\\n01364| \\\\tif weapon != null and weapon.has_method(\\\\\\\"GetMagazineMaxCounts\\\\\\\"):\\\\n01365| \\\\t\\\\tmag_max_counts = Array(weapon.GetMagazineMaxCounts())\\\\n01366| \\\\n01367| \\\\tvar parts: Array = []\\\\n01368| \\\\t# Current magazine always shown in brackets\\\\n01369| \\\\tparts.append(\\\\\\\"[%d]\\\\\\\" % magazine_ammo_counts[0])\\\\n01370| \\\\n01371| \\\\t# Spare magazines: skip empty, show partial individually, abbreviate full as + xN\\\\n01372| \\\\tvar full_spare_count: int = 0\\\\n01373| \\\\tfor i in range(1, magazine_ammo_counts.size()):\\\\n01374| \\\\t\\\\tvar ammo: int = magazine_ammo_counts[i]\\\\n01375| \\\\t\\\\tif ammo <= 0:\\\\n01376| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tcontinue\\\\n01377| \\\\t\\\\tvar cap: int = mag_max_counts[i] if i < mag_max_counts.size() else 0\\\\n01378| \\\\t\\\\tif cap > 0 and ammo >= cap:\\\\n01379| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tfull_spare_count += 1\\\\n01380| \\\\t\\\\telse:\\\\n01381| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tparts.append(\\\\\\\"%d\\\\\\\" % ammo)\\\\n01382| \\\\n01383| \\\\tif full_spare_count > 0:\\\\n01384| \\\\t\\\\tparts.append(\\\\\\\"+ x%d\\\\\\\" % full_spare_count)\\\\n01385| \\\\n01386| \\\\t_magazines_label.text = \\\\\\\"MAGS: \\\\\\\" + \\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\".join(parts)\\\\n01387| \\\\n01388| \\\\n01389| ## Update the enemy count label in UI.\\\\n01390| func _update_enemy_count_label() -> void:\\\\n01391| \\\\tif _enemy_count_label:\\\\n01392| \\\\t\\\\t_enemy_count_label.text = \\\\\\\"Enemies: %d\\\\\\\" % _current_enemy_count\\\\n01393| \\\\n01394| \\\\n01395| ## Show death message when player dies.\\\\n01396| func _show_death_message() -> void:\\\\n01397| \\\\tif _game_over_shown:\\\\n01398| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n01399| \\\\n01400| \\\\t_game_over_shown = true\\\\n01401| \\\\n01402| \\\\tvar ui := get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"CanvasLayer/UI\\\\\\\")\\\\n01403| \\\\tif ui == null:\\\\n01404| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n01405| \\\\n01406| \\\\tvar death_label := Label.new()\\\\n01407| \\\\tdeath_label.name = \\\\\\\"DeathLabel\\\\\\\"\\\\n01408| \\\\tdeath_label.text = \\\\\\\"YOU DIED\\\\\\\"\\\\n01409| \\\\tdeath_label.horizontal_alignment = HORIZONTAL_ALIGNMENT_CENTER\\\\n01410| \\\\tdeath_label.vertical_alignment = VERTICAL_ALIGNMENT_CENTER\\\\n01411| \\\\tdeath_label.add_theme_font_size_override(\\\\\\\"font_size\\\\\\\", 64)\\\\n01412| \\\\tdeath_label.add_theme_color_override(\\\\\\\"font_color\\\\\\\", Color(1.0, 0.15, 0.15, 1.0))\\\\n01413| \\\\n01414| \\\\t# Center the label\\\\n01415| \\\\tdeath_label.set_anchors_preset(Control.PRESET_CENTER)\\\\n01416| \\\\tdeath_label.offset_left = -200\\\\n01417| \\\\tdeath_label.offset_right = 200\\\\n01418| \\\\tdeath_label.offset_top = -50\\\\n01419| \\\\tdeath_label.offset_bottom = 50\\\\n01420| \\\\n01421| \\\\tui.add_child(death_label)\\\\n01422| \\\\n01423| \\\\n01424| ## Show victory message when all enemies are eliminated.\\\\n01425| func _show_victory_message() -> void:\\\\n01426| \\\\tvar ui := get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"CanvasLayer/UI\\\\\\\")\\\\n01427| \\\\tif ui == null:\\\\n01428| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n01429| \\\\n01430| \\\\tvar victory_label := Label.new()\\\\n01431| \\\\tvictory_label.name = \\\\\\\"VictoryLabel\\\\\\\"\\\\n01432| \\\\tvictory_label.text = \\\\\\\"BUILDING CLEARED!\\\\\\\"\\\\n01433| \\\\tvictory_label.horizontal_alignment = HORIZONTAL_ALIGNMENT_CENTER\\\\n01434| \\\\tvictory_label.vertical_alignment = VERTICAL_ALIGNMENT_CENTER\\\\n01435| \\\\tvictory_label.add_theme_font_size_override(\\\\\\\"font_size\\\\\\\", 48)\\\\n01436| \\\\tvictory_label.add_theme_color_override(\\\\\\\"font_color\\\\\\\", Color(0.2, 1.0, 0.3, 1.0))\\\\n01437| \\\\n01438| \\\\t# Center the label\\\\n01439| \\\\tvictory_label.set_anchors_preset(Control.PRESET_CENTER)\\\\n01440| \\\\tvictory_label.offset_left = -200\\\\n01441| \\\\tvictory_label.offset_right = 200\\\\n01442| \\\\tvictory_label.offset_top = -50\\\\n01443| \\\\tvictory_label.offset_bottom = 50\\\\n01444| \\\\n01445| \\\\tui.add_child(victory_label)\\\\n01446| \\\\n01447| \\\\t# Show final stats\\\\n01448| \\\\tvar stats_label := Label.new()\\\\n01449| \\\\tstats_label.name = \\\\\\\"StatsLabel\\\\\\\"\\\\n01450| \\\\tif GameManager:\\\\n01451| \\\\t\\\\tstats_label.text = \\\\\\\"Kills: %d | Accuracy: %.1f%%\\\\\\\" % [GameManager.kills, GameManager.get_accuracy()]\\\\n01452| \\\\telse:\\\\n01453| \\\\t\\\\tstats_label.text = \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n01454| \\\\tstats_label.horizontal_alignment = HORIZONTAL_ALIGNMENT_CENTER\\\\n01455| \\\\tstats_label.vertical_alignment = VERTICAL_ALIGNMENT_CENTER\\\\n01456| \\\\tstats_label.add_theme_font_size_override(\\\\\\\"font_size\\\\\\\", 24)\\\\n01457| \\\\tstats_label.add_theme_color_override(\\\\\\\"font_color\\\\\\\", Color(0.8, 0.9, 0.8, 1.0))\\\\n01458| \\\\n01459| \\\\t# Position below victory message\\\\n01460| \\\\tstats_label.set_anchors_preset(Control.PRESET_CENTER)\\\\n01461| \\\\tstats_label.offset_left = -200\\\\n01462| \\\\tstats_label.offset_right = 200\\\\n01463| \\\\tstats_label.offset_top = 50\\\\n01464| \\\\tstats_label.offset_bottom = 100\\\\n01465| \\\\n01466| \\\\tui.add_child(stats_label)\\\\n01467| \\\\n01468| \\\\n01469| ## Show the animated score screen with Hotline Miami 2 style effects (Issue #415).\\\\n01470| ## Uses the AnimatedScoreScreen component for sequential reveal and counting animations.\\\\n01471| ## After animations complete, adds replay and restart buttons (Issue #416).\\\\n01472| ## @param score_data: Dictionary containing all score components from ScoreManager.\\\\n01473| func _show_score_screen(score_data: Dictionary) -> void:\\\\n01474| \\\\tvar ui := get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"CanvasLayer/UI\\\\\\\")\\\\n01475| \\\\tif ui == null:\\\\n01476| \\\\t\\\\t_show_victory_message()  # Fallback\\\\n01477| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n01478| \\\\n01479| \\\\t# Load and use the animated score screen component\\\\n01480| \\\\tvar animated_score_screen_script = load(\\\\\\\"res://scripts/ui/animated_score_screen.gd\\\\\\\")\\\\n01481| \\\\tif animated_score_screen_script:\\\\n01482| \\\\t\\\\tvar score_screen = animated_score_screen_script.new()\\\\n01483| \\\\t\\\\tadd_child(score_screen)\\\\n01484| \\\\t\\\\t# Connect to animation_completed to add replay/restart buttons after animation\\\\n01485| \\\\t\\\\tscore_screen.animation_completed.connect(_on_score_animation_completed)\\\\n01486| \\\\t\\\\tscore_screen.show_animated_score(ui, score_data)\\\\n01487| \\\\telse:\\\\n01488| \\\\t\\\\t# Fallback to simple display if animated script not found\\\\n01489| \\\\t\\\\t_show_fallback_score_screen(ui, score_data)\\\\n01490| \\\\n01491| \\\\n01492| ## Called when the animated score screen finishes all animations.\\\\n01493| ## Adds replay and restart buttons to the score screen container.\\\\n01494| func _on_score_animation_completed(container: VBoxContainer) -> void:\\\\n01495| \\\\t_add_score_screen_buttons(container)\\\\n01496| \\\\n01497| \\\\n01498| ## Fallback score screen if animated component is not available.\\\\n01499| func _show_fallback_score_screen(ui: Control, score_data: Dictionary) -> void:\\\\n01500| \\\\t# Load Gothic bitmap font for score screen labels\\\\n01501| \\\\tvar gothic_font = load(\\\\\\\"res://assets/fonts/gothic_bitmap.fnt\\\\\\\")\\\\n01502| \\\\tvar _font_loaded := gothic_font != null\\\\n01503| \\\\n01504| \\\\tvar background := ColorRect.new()\\\\n01505| \\\\tbackground.name = \\\\\\\"ScoreBackground\\\\\\\"\\\\n01506| \\\\tbackground.color = Color(0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.7)\\\\n01507| \\\\tbackground.set_anchors_preset(Control.PRESET_FULL_RECT)\\\\n01508| \\\\tbackground.mouse_filter = Control.MOUSE_FILTER_IGNORE\\\\n01509| \\\\tui.add_child(background)\\\\n01510| \\\\n01511| \\\\tvar container := VBoxContainer.new()\\\\n01512| \\\\tcontainer.name = \\\\\\\"ScoreContainer\\\\\\\"\\\\n01513| \\\\tcontainer.set_anchors_preset(Control.PRESET_CENTER)\\\\n01514| \\\\tcontainer.offset_left = -300\\\\n01515| \\\\tcontainer.offset_right = 300\\\\n01516| \\\\tcontainer.offset_top = -200\\\\n01517| \\\\tcontainer.offset_bottom = 200\\\\n01518| \\\\tcontainer.add_theme_constant_override(\\\\\\\"separation\\\\\\\", 8)\\\\n01519| \\\\tui.add_child(container)\\\\n01520| \\\\n01521| \\\\tvar title_label := Label.new()\\\\n01522| \\\\ttitle_label.text = \\\\\\\"LEVEL CLEARED!\\\\\\\"\\\\n01523| \\\\ttitle_label.horizontal_alignment = HORIZONTAL_ALIGNMENT_CENTER\\\\n01524| \\\\ttitle_label.add_theme_font_size_override(\\\\\\\"font_size\\\\\\\", 42)\\\\n01525| \\\\ttitle_label.add_theme_color_override(\\\\\\\"font_color\\\\\\\", Color(0.2, 1.0, 0.3, 1.0))\\\\n01526| \\\\tcontainer.add_child(title_label)\\\\n01527| \\\\n01528| \\\\tvar rank_label := Label.new()\\\\n01529| \\\\trank_label.text = \\\\\\\"RANK: %s\\\\\\\" % score_data.rank\\\\n01530| \\\\trank_label.horizontal_alignment = HORIZONTAL_ALIGNMENT_CENTER\\\\n01531| \\\\trank_label.add_theme_font_size_override(\\\\\\\"font_size\\\\\\\", 64)\\\\n01532| \\\\trank_label.add_theme_color_override(\\\\\\\"font_color\\\\\\\", _get_rank_color(score_data.rank))\\\\n01533| \\\\tif _font_loaded:\\\\n01534| \\\\t\\\\trank_label.add_theme_font_override(\\\\\\\"font\\\\\\\", gothic_font)\\\\n01535| \\\\tcontainer.add_child(rank_label)\\\\n01536| \\\\n01537| \\\\tvar total_label := Label.new()\\\\n01538| \\\\ttotal_label.text = \\\\\\\"TOTAL SCORE: %d\\\\\\\" % score_data.total_score\\\\n01539| \\\\ttotal_label.horizontal_alignment = HORIZONTAL_ALIGNMENT_CENTER\\\\n01540| \\\\ttotal_label.add_theme_font_size_override(\\\\\\\"font_size\\\\\\\", 32)\\\\n01541| \\\\ttotal_label.add_theme_color_override(\\\\\\\"font_color\\\\\\\", Color(1.0, 0.9, 0.3, 1.0))\\\\n01542| \\\\tcontainer.add_child(total_label)\\\\n01543| \\\\n01544| \\\\t# Add replay and restart buttons to fallback screen\\\\n01545| \\\\t_add_score_screen_buttons(container)\\\\n01546| \\\\n01547| \\\\n01548| ## Adds Restart, Next Level, Level Select, and Watch Replay buttons to a score screen container.\\\\n01549| ## Issue #568: Added Next Level and Level Select buttons after final grade.\\\\n01550| func _add_score_screen_buttons(container: VBoxContainer) -> void:\\\\n01551| \\\\t_score_shown = true\\\\n01552| \\\\n01553| \\\\t# Add spacer\\\\n01554| \\\\tvar spacer := Control.new()\\\\n01555| \\\\tspacer.custom_minimum_size.y = 10\\\\n01556| \\\\tcontainer.add_child(spacer)\\\\n01557| \\\\n01558| \\\\t# Add buttons container (vertical layout)\\\\n01559| \\\\tvar buttons_container := VBoxContainer.new()\\\\n01560| \\\\tbuttons_container.name = \\\\\\\"ButtonsContainer\\\\\\\"\\\\n01561| \\\\tbuttons_container.alignment = BoxContainer.ALIGNMENT_CENTER\\\\n01562| \\\\tbuttons_container.add_theme_constant_override(\\\\\\\"separation\\\\\\\", 10)\\\\n01563| \\\\tcontainer.add_child(buttons_container)\\\\n01564| \\\\n01565| \\\\t# Next Level button (Issue #568)\\\\n01566| \\\\tvar next_level_path: String = _get_next_level_path()\\\\n01567| \\\\tif next_level_path != \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\":\\\\n01568| \\\\t\\\\tvar next_button := Button.new()\\\\n01569| \\\\t\\\\tnext_button.name = \\\\\\\"NextLevelButton\\\\\\\"\\\\n01570| \\\\t\\\\tnext_button.text = \\\\\\\"→ Next Level\\\\\\\"\\\\n01571| \\\\t\\\\tnext_button.custom_minimum_size = Vector2(200, 40)\\\\n01572| \\\\t\\\\tnext_button.add_theme_font_size_override(\\\\\\\"font_size\\\\\\\", 18)\\\\n01573| \\\\t\\\\tnext_button.pressed.connect(_on_next_level_pressed.bind(next_level_path))\\\\n01574| \\\\t\\\\tbuttons_container.add_child(next_button)\\\\n01575| \\\\n01576| \\\\t# Restart button\\\\n01577| \\\\tvar restart_button := Button.new()\\\\n01578| \\\\trestart_button.name = \\\\\\\"RestartButton\\\\\\\"\\\\n01579| \\\\trestart_button.text = \\\\\\\"↻ Restart (Q)\\\\\\\"\\\\n01580| \\\\trestart_button.custom_minimum_size = Vector2(200, 40)\\\\n01581| \\\\trestart_button.add_theme_font_size_override(\\\\\\\"font_size\\\\\\\", 18)\\\\n01582| \\\\trestart_button.pressed.connect(_on_restart_pressed)\\\\n01583| \\\\tbuttons_container.add_child(restart_button)\\\\n01584| \\\\n01585| \\\\t# Level Select button (Issue #568)\\\\n01586| \\\\tvar level_select_button := Button.new()\\\\n01587| \\\\tlevel_select_button.name = \\\\\\\"LevelSelectButton\\\\\\\"\\\\n01588| \\\\tlevel_select_button.text = \\\\\\\"☰ Level Select\\\\\\\"\\\\n01589| \\\\tlevel_select_button.custom_minimum_size = Vector2(200, 40)\\\\n01590| \\\\tlevel_select_button.add_theme_font_size_override(\\\\\\\"font_size\\\\\\\", 18)\\\\n01591| \\\\tlevel_select_button.pressed.connect(_on_level_select_pressed)\\\\n01592| \\\\tbuttons_container.add_child(level_select_button)\\\\n01593| \\\\n01594| \\\\t# Watch Replay button (Issue #807: only shown if replay viewing is enabled in experimental settings)\\\\n01595| \\\\tvar experimental_settings: Node = get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"/root/ExperimentalSettings\\\\\\\")\\\\n01596| \\\\tvar replay_enabled: bool = experimental_settings != null and experimental_settings.has_method(\\\\\\\"is_replay_enabled\\\\\\\") and experimental_settings.is_replay_enabled()\\\\n01597| \\\\n01598| \\\\tif replay_enabled:\\\\n01599| \\\\t\\\\tvar replay_button := Button.new()\\\\n01600| \\\\t\\\\treplay_button.name = \\\\\\\"ReplayButton\\\\\\\"\\\\n01601| \\\\t\\\\treplay_button.text = \\\\\\\"▶ Watch Replay (W)\\\\\\\"\\\\n01602| \\\\t\\\\treplay_button.custom_minimum_size = Vector2(200, 40)\\\\n01603| \\\\t\\\\treplay_button.add_theme_font_size_override(\\\\\\\"font_size\\\\\\\", 18)\\\\n01604| \\\\n01605| \\\\t\\\\t# Check if replay data is available\\\\n01606| \\\\t\\\\tvar replay_manager: Node = _get_or_create_replay_manager()\\\\n01607| \\\\t\\\\tvar has_replay_data: bool = replay_manager != null and replay_manager.has_method(\\\\\\\"HasReplay\\\\\\\") and replay_manager.HasReplay()\\\\n01608| \\\\n01609| \\\\t\\\\tif has_replay_data:\\\\n01610| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\treplay_button.pressed.connect(_on_watch_replay_pressed)\\\\n01611| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"Watch Replay button created (replay data available)\\\\\\\")\\\\n01612| \\\\t\\\\telse:\\\\n01613| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\treplay_button.disabled = true\\\\n01614| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\treplay_button.text = \\\\\\\"▶ Watch Replay (W) - no data\\\\\\\"\\\\n01615| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\treplay_button.tooltip_text = \\\\\\\"Replay recording was not available for this session\\\\\\\"\\\\n01616| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"Watch Replay button created (disabled - no replay data)\\\\\\\")\\\\n01617| \\\\n01618| \\\\t\\\\tbuttons_container.add_child(replay_button)\\\\n01619| \\\\telse:\\\\n01620| \\\\t\\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"Watch Replay button not shown (replay viewing disabled in experimental settings)\\\\\\\")\\\\n01621| \\\\n01622| \\\\t# Armory button (Issue #897: shown highlighted when items are available to unlock; Issue #1622: always shown)\\\\n01623| \\\\tvar unlock_manager: Node = get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"/root/UnlockManager\\\\\\\")\\\\n01624| \\\\tvar armory_button := Button.new()\\\\n01625| \\\\tarmory_button.name = \\\\\\\"ArmoryButton\\\\\\\"\\\\n01626| \\\\tarmory_button.pressed.connect(_on_armory_button_pressed)\\\\n01627| \\\\tbuttons_container.add_child(armory_button)\\\\n01628| \\\\tvar has_available_unlock: bool = unlock_manager != null and unlock_manager.has_method(\\\\\\\"has_any_available_unlock\\\\\\\") and unlock_manager.has_any_available_unlock()\\\\n01629| \\\\tif has_available_unlock:\\\\n01630| \\\\t\\\\tarmory_button.text = \\\\\\\"★ Armory — Items Available!\\\\\\\"\\\\n01631| \\\\t\\\\tarmory_button.custom_minimum_size = Vector2(200, 40)\\\\n01632| \\\\t\\\\tarmory_button.add_theme_font_size_override(\\\\\\\"font_size\\\\\\\", 18)\\\\n01633| \\\\t\\\\tarmory_button.add_theme_color_override(\\\\\\\"font_color\\\\\\\", Color(1.0, 0.85, 0.2, 1.0))\\\\n01634| \\\\t\\\\tvar armory_style := StyleBoxFlat.new()\\\\n01635| \\\\t\\\\tarmory_style.bg_color = Color(0.28, 0.22, 0.08, 0.9)\\\\n01636| \\\\t\\\\tarmory_style.border_color = Color(1.0, 0.8, 0.1, 1.0)\\\\n01637| \\\\t\\\\tarmory_style.border_width_left = 2\\\\n01638| \\\\t\\\\tarmory_style.border_width_right = 2\\\\n01639| \\\\t\\\\tarmory_style.border_width_top = 2\\\\n01640| \\\\t\\\\tarmory_style.border_width_bottom = 2\\\\n01641| \\\\t\\\\tarmory_style.corner_radius_top_left = 4\\\\n01642| \\\\t\\\\tarmory_style.corner_radius_top_right = 4\\\\n01643| \\\\t\\\\tarmory_style.corner_radius_bottom_left = 4\\\\n01644| \\\\t\\\\tarmory_style.corner_radius_bottom_right = 4\\\\n01645| \\\\t\\\\tarmory_button.add_theme_stylebox_override(\\\\\\\"normal\\\\\\\", armory_style)\\\\n01646| \\\\t\\\\t# Add gold shine shader overlay (Issue #1536).\\\\n01647| \\\\t\\\\tvar _armory_shine_shader := load(\\\\\\\"res://scripts/shaders/gold_shine.gdshader\\\\\\\") as Shader\\\\n01648| \\\\t\\\\tif _armory_shine_shader:\\\\n01649| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar _armory_shine_mat := ShaderMaterial.new()\\\\n01650| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_armory_shine_mat.shader = _armory_shine_shader\\\\n01651| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar _armory_shine_overlay := ColorRect.new()\\\\n01652| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_armory_shine_overlay.name = \\\\\\\"ArmoryGoldShineOverlay\\\\\\\"\\\\n01653| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_armory_shine_overlay.set_anchors_and_offsets_preset(Control.PRESET_FULL_RECT)\\\\n01654| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_armory_shine_overlay.mouse_filter = Control.MOUSE_FILTER_IGNORE\\\\n01655| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_armory_shine_overlay.material = _armory_shine_mat\\\\n01656| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tarmory_button.add_child(_armory_shine_overlay)\\\\n01657| \\\\telse:\\\\n01658| \\\\t\\\\tarmory_button.text = \\\\\\\"Armory\\\\\\\"\\\\n01659| \\\\n01660| \\\\t# Show cursor for button interaction\\\\n01661| \\\\tInput.set_mouse_mode(Input.MOUSE_MODE_CONFINED)\\\\n01662| \\\\n01663| \\\\t# Focus the next level button if available, otherwise restart\\\\n01664| \\\\tif next_level_path != \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\":\\\\n01665| \\\\t\\\\tbuttons_container.get_node(\\\\\\\"NextLevelButton\\\\\\\").grab_focus()\\\\n01666| \\\\telse:\\\\n01667| \\\\t\\\\trestart_button.grab_focus()\\\\n01668| \\\\n01669| \\\\n01670| ## Get the color for a given rank.\\\\n01671| func _get_rank_color(rank: String) -> Color:\\\\n01672| \\\\tmatch rank:\\\\n01673| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\"S\\\\\\\":\\\\n01674| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\treturn Color(1.0, 0.84, 0.0, 1.0)  # Gold\\\\n01675| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\"A+\\\\\\\":\\\\n01676| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\treturn Color(0.0, 1.0, 0.5, 1.0)  # Bright green\\\\n01677| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\"A\\\\\\\":\\\\n01678| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\treturn Color(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1.0)  # Green\\\\n01679| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\"B\\\\\\\":\\\\n01680| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\treturn Color(0.3, 0.7, 1.0, 1.0)  # Blue\\\\n01681| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\"C\\\\\\\":\\\\n01682| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\treturn Color(1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0)  # White\\\\n01683| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\"D\\\\\\\":\\\\n01684| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\treturn Color(1.0, 0.6, 0.2, 1.0)  # Orange\\\\n01685| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\"F\\\\\\\":\\\\n01686| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\treturn Color(1.0, 0.2, 0.2, 1.0)  # Red\\\\n01687| \\\\t\\\\t_:\\\\n01688| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\treturn Color(1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0)  # Default white\\\\n01689| \\\\n01690| \\\\n01691| ## Show game over message when player runs out of ammo with enemies remaining.\\\\n01692| func _show_game_over_message() -> void:\\\\n01693| \\\\t_game_over_shown = true\\\\n01694| \\\\n01695| \\\\tvar ui := get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"CanvasLayer/UI\\\\\\\")\\\\n01696| \\\\tif ui == null:\\\\n01697| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n01698| \\\\n01699| \\\\tvar game_over_label := Label.new()\\\\n01700| \\\\tgame_over_label.name = \\\\\\\"GameOverLabel\\\\\\\"\\\\n01701| \\\\tgame_over_label.text = \\\\\\\"OUT OF AMMO\\\\\\\\n%d enemies remaining\\\\\\\" % _current_enemy_count\\\\n01702| \\\\tgame_over_label.horizontal_alignment = HORIZONTAL_ALIGNMENT_CENTER\\\\n01703| \\\\tgame_over_label.vertical_alignment = VERTICAL_ALIGNMENT_CENTER\\\\n01704| \\\\tgame_over_label.add_theme_font_size_override(\\\\\\\"font_size\\\\\\\", 48)\\\\n01705| \\\\tgame_over_label.add_theme_color_override(\\\\\\\"font_color\\\\\\\", Color(1.0, 0.2, 0.2, 1.0))\\\\n01706| \\\\n01707| \\\\t# Center the label\\\\n01708| \\\\tgame_over_label.set_anchors_preset(Control.PRESET_CENTER)\\\\n01709| \\\\tgame_over_label.offset_left = -250\\\\n01710| \\\\tgame_over_label.offset_right = 250\\\\n01711| \\\\tgame_over_label.offset_top = -75\\\\n01712| \\\\tgame_over_label.offset_bottom = 75\\\\n01713| \\\\n01714| \\\\tui.add_child(game_over_label)\\\\n01715| \\\\n01716| \\\\n01717| ## Setup the weapon based on GameManager's selected weapon.\\\\n01718| ## Removes the default MakarovPM and loads the selected weapon if different.\\\\n01719| func _setup_selected_weapon() -> void:\\\\n01720| \\\\tif _player == null:\\\\n01721| \\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n01722| \\\\n01723| \\\\t# Get selected weapon from GameManager\\\\n01724| \\\\tvar selected_weapon_id: String = \\\\\\\"makarov_pm\\\\\\\"  # Default\\\\n01725| \\\\tif GameManager:\\\\n01726| \\\\t\\\\tselected_weapon_id = GameManager.get_selected_weapon()\\\\n01727| \\\\n01728| \\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"Setting up weapon: %s\\\\\\\" % selected_weapon_id)\\\\n01729| \\\\n01730| \\\\t# Check if C# Player already equipped the correct weapon (via ApplySelectedWeaponFromGameManager)\\\\n01731| \\\\t# This prevents double-equipping when both C# and GDScript weapon setup run\\\\n01732| \\\\t# BUT we still need to apply building-level ammo configuration (Issue #949)\\\\n01733| \\\\tif selected_weapon_id != \\\\\\\"makarov_pm\\\\\\\":\\\\n01734| \\\\t\\\\tvar weapon_names: Dictionary = {\\\\n01735| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\"shotgun\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Shotgun\\\\\\\",\\\\n01736| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\"mini_uzi\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"MiniUzi\\\\\\\",\\\\n01737| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\"silenced_pistol\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SilencedPistol\\\\\\\",\\\\n01738| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\"sniper\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SniperRifle\\\\\\\",\\\\n01739| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\"m16\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"AssaultRifle\\\\\\\",\\\\n01740| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\"ak_gl\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"AKGL\\\\\\\",\\\\n01741| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\"revolver\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Revolver\\\\\\\"\\\\n01742| \\\\t\\\\t}\\\\n01743| \\\\t\\\\tif selected_weapon_id in weapon_names:\\\\n01744| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar expected_name: String = weapon_names[selected_weapon_id]\\\\n01745| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar existing_weapon = _player.get_node_or_null(expected_name)\\\\n01746| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tif existing_weapon != null and _player.get(\\\\\\\"CurrentWeapon\\\\\\\") == existing_weapon:\\\\n01747| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_log_to_file(\\\\\\\"%s already equipped by C# Player - applying building-level ammo config\\\\\\\" % expected_name)\\\\n01748| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t# Apply building-level ammo configuration to already-equipped weapon (Issue #949)\\\\n01749| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_apply_building_ammo_config(existing_weapon, selected_weapon_id)\\\\n01750| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\treturn\\\\n01751| \\\\n01752| \\\\t# If shotgun is selected, we need to swap weapons\\\\n01753| \\\\tif selected_weapon_id == \\\\\\\"shotgun\\\\\\\":\\\\n01754| \\\\t\\\\t# Remove the default MakarovPM\\\\n01755| \\\\t\\\\tvar makarov = _player.get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"MakarovPM\\\\\\\")\\\\n01756| \\\\t\\\\tif makarov:\\\\n01757| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tmakarov.queue_free()\\\\n01758| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"BuildingLevel: Removed default MakarovPM\\\\\\\")\\\\n01759| \\\\n01760| \\\\t\\\\t# Load and add the shotgun\\\\n01761| \\\\t\\\\tvar shotgun_scene = load(\\\\\\\"res://scenes/weapons/csharp/Shotgun.tscn\\\\\\\")\\\\n01762| \\\\t\\\\tif shotgun_scene:\\\\n01763| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar shotgun = shotgun_scene.instantiate()\\\\n01764| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tshotgun.name = \\\\\\\"Shotgun\\\\\\\"\\\\n01765| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_player.add_child(shotgun)\\\\n01766| \\\\n01767| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t# Set the CurrentWeapon reference in C# Player\\\\n01768| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tif _player.has_method(\\\\\\\"EquipWeapon\\\\\\\"):\\\\n01769| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_player.EquipWeapon(shotgun)\\\\n01770| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\telif _player.get(\\\\\\\"CurrentWeapon\\\\\\\") != null:\\\\n01771| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_player.CurrentWeapon = shotgun\\\\n01772| \\\\n01773| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"BuildingLevel: Shotgun equipped successfully\\\\\\\")\\\\n01774| \\\\t\\\\telse:\\\\n01775| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tpush_error(\\\\\\\"BuildingLevel: Failed to load Shotgun scene!\\\\\\\")\\\\n01776| \\\\t# If Mini UZI is selected, swap weapons\\\\n01777| \\\\telif selected_weapon_id == \\\\\\\"mini_uzi\\\\\\\":\\\\n01778| \\\\t\\\\t# Remove the default MakarovPM\\\\n01779| \\\\t\\\\tvar makarov = _player.get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"MakarovPM\\\\\\\")\\\\n01780| \\\\t\\\\tif makarov:\\\\n01781| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tmakarov.queue_free()\\\\n01782| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"BuildingLevel: Removed default MakarovPM\\\\\\\")\\\\n01783| \\\\n01784| \\\\t\\\\t# Load and add the Mini UZI\\\\n01785| \\\\t\\\\tvar mini_uzi_scene = load(\\\\\\\"res://scenes/weapons/csharp/MiniUzi.tscn\\\\\\\")\\\\n01786| \\\\t\\\\tif mini_uzi_scene:\\\\n01787| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar mini_uzi = mini_uzi_scene.instantiate()\\\\n01788| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tmini_uzi.name = \\\\\\\"MiniUzi\\\\\\\"\\\\n01789| \\\\n01790| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t# Reduce Mini UZI ammunition by half for Building level (issue #413)\\\\n01791| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t# Set StartingMagazineCount to 2 BEFORE adding to scene tree\\\\n01792| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t# This ensures magazines are initialized with correct count when _Ready() is called\\\\n01793| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tif mini_uzi.get(\\\\\\\"StartingMagazineCount\\\\\\\") != null:\\\\n01794| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tmini_uzi.StartingMagazineCount = 2\\\\n01795| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"BuildingLevel: Mini UZI StartingMagazineCount set to 2 (before initialization)\\\\\\\")\\\\n01796| \\\\n01797| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_player.add_child(mini_uzi)\\\\n01798| \\\\n01799| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t# Set the CurrentWeapon reference in C# Player\\\\n01800| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tif _player.has_method(\\\\\\\"EquipWeapon\\\\\\\"):\\\\n01801| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_player.EquipWeapon(mini_uzi)\\\\n01802| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\telif _player.get(\\\\\\\"CurrentWeapon\\\\\\\") != null:\\\\n01803| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_player.CurrentWeapon = mini_uzi\\\\n01804| \\\\n01805| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"BuildingLevel: Mini UZI equipped successfully\\\\\\\")\\\\n01806| \\\\t\\\\telse:\\\\n01807| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tpush_error(\\\\\\\"BuildingLevel: Failed to load MiniUzi scene!\\\\\\\")\\\\n01808| \\\\t# If Silenced Pistol is selected, swap weapons\\\\n01809| \\\\telif selected_weapon_id == \\\\\\\"silenced_pistol\\\\\\\":\\\\n01810| \\\\t\\\\t# Remove the default MakarovPM\\\\n01811| \\\\t\\\\tvar makarov = _player.get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"MakarovPM\\\\\\\")\\\\n01812| \\\\t\\\\tif makarov:\\\\n01813| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tmakarov.queue_free()\\\\n01814| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"BuildingLevel: Removed default MakarovPM\\\\\\\")\\\\n01815| \\\\n01816| \\\\t\\\\t# Load and add the Silenced Pistol\\\\n01817| \\\\t\\\\tvar pistol_scene = load(\\\\\\\"res://scenes/weapons/csharp/SilencedPistol.tscn\\\\\\\")\\\\n01818| \\\\t\\\\tif pistol_scene:\\\\n01819| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar pistol = pistol_scene.instantiate()\\\\n01820| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tpistol.name = \\\\\\\"SilencedPistol\\\\\\\"\\\\n01821| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_player.add_child(pistol)\\\\n01822| \\\\n01823| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t# Set the CurrentWeapon reference in C# Player\\\\n01824| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tif _player.has_method(\\\\\\\"EquipWeapon\\\\\\\"):\\\\n01825| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_player.EquipWeapon(pistol)\\\\n01826| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\telif _player.get(\\\\\\\"CurrentWeapon\\\\\\\") != null:\\\\n01827| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_player.CurrentWeapon = pistol\\\\n01828| \\\\n01829| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"BuildingLevel: Silenced Pistol equipped successfully\\\\\\\")\\\\n01830| \\\\t\\\\telse:\\\\n01831| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tpush_error(\\\\\\\"BuildingLevel: Failed to load SilencedPistol scene!\\\\\\\")\\\\n01832| \\\\t# If Sniper Rifle (ASVK) is selected, swap weapons\\\\n01833| \\\\telif selected_weapon_id == \\\\\\\"sniper\\\\\\\":\\\\n01834| \\\\t\\\\t# Remove the default MakarovPM\\\\n01835| \\\\t\\\\tvar makarov = _player.get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"MakarovPM\\\\\\\")\\\\n01836| \\\\t\\\\tif makarov:\\\\n01837| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tmakarov.queue_free()\\\\n01838| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"BuildingLevel: Removed default MakarovPM\\\\\\\")\\\\n01839| \\\\n01840| \\\\t\\\\t# Load and add the Sniper Rifle\\\\n01841| \\\\t\\\\tvar sniper_scene = load(\\\\\\\"res://scenes/weapons/csharp/SniperRifle.tscn\\\\\\\")\\\\n01842| \\\\t\\\\tif sniper_scene:\\\\n01843| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar sniper = sniper_scene.instantiate()\\\\n01844| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tsniper.name = \\\\\\\"SniperRifle\\\\\\\"\\\\n01845| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_player.add_child(sniper)\\\\n01846| \\\\n01847| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t# Set the CurrentWeapon reference in C# Player\\\\n01848| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tif _player.has_method(\\\\\\\"EquipWeapon\\\\\\\"):\\\\n01849| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_player.EquipWeapon(sniper)\\\\n01850| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\telif _player.get(\\\\\\\"CurrentWeapon\\\\\\\") != null:\\\\n01851| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_player.CurrentWeapon = sniper\\\\n01852| \\\\n01853| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"BuildingLevel: ASVK Sniper Rifle equipped successfully\\\\\\\")\\\\n01854| \\\\t\\\\telse:\\\\n01855| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tpush_error(\\\\\\\"BuildingLevel: Failed to load SniperRifle scene!\\\\\\\")\\\\n01856| \\\\t# If M16 (assault rifle) is selected, swap weapons\\\\n01857| \\\\telif selected_weapon_id == \\\\\\\"m16\\\\\\\":\\\\n01858| \\\\t\\\\t# Remove the default MakarovPM\\\\n01859| \\\\t\\\\tvar makarov = _player.get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"MakarovPM\\\\\\\")\\\\n01860| \\\\t\\\\tif makarov:\\\\n01861| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tmakarov.queue_free()\\\\n01862| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tprint(\\\\\\\"BuildingLevel: Removed default MakarovPM\\\\\\\")\\\\n01863| \\\\n01864| \\\\t\\\\t# Load and add the Assault Rifle\\\\n01865| \\\\t\\\\tvar m16_scene = load(\\\\\\\"res://scenes/weapons/csharp/AssaultRifle.tscn\\\\\\\")\\\\n01866| \\\\t\\\\tif m16_scene:\\\\n01867| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar m16 = m16_scene.instantiate()\\\\n01868| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tm16.name = \\\\\\\"AssaultRifle\\\\\\\"\\\\n01869| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_player.add_child(m16)\\\\n01870| \\\\n01871| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t# Set the CurrentWeapon reference in C# Player\\\\n01872| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tif _player.has_method(\\\\\\\"EquipWeapon\\\\\\\"):\\\\n01873| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_player.EquipWeapon(m16)\\\\n01874| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\telif _player.get(\\\\\\\"CurrentWeapon\\\\\\\") != null:\\\\n01875| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_player.CurrentWeapon = m16\\\\n01876| \\\\n01877| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t# Reduce M16 ammunition by half for Building level (issue #413)\\\\n01878| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t# In Power Fantasy mode, apply ammo multiplier (issue #501)\\\\n01879| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar base_magazines: int = 2\\\\n01880| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar difficulty_manager: Node = get_node_or_null(\\\\\\\"/root/DifficultyManager\\\\\\\")\\\\n01881| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\tif difficulty_manager:\\\\n01882| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tvar ammo_multiplier: int = difficulty_manager.get_ammo_multiplier()\\\\n01883| \\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tif ammo_multipli